\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-South African rand slumps after \uc2 Moody's\uc2  warning, stocks tumble\b0\par\par\uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2018\par 17:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Rand slumps more than 3 percent vs dollar\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on rand\par \par \uc2 * Yields on government bonds rise\par \par \uc2 * Stocks fall more than 3 percent as \uc2 Naspers\uc2  tumbles (Updates with bonds, stocks closing prices)\par \par \uc2 By Alexander Winning and Olivia Kumwenda-Mtambo\par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, Aug 15 (Reuters) - South Africa's rand slumped on Wednesday as ratings agency \uc2 Moody's\uc2  warned that the pace of fiscal consolidation in Africa's most industrialised nation had slowed and retail sales data disappointed, underlining the fragility of the economy.\par \par \uc2 Moody's\uc2  is the only one of the "big three" ratings agencies which still has South Africa's sovereign rating in investment grade, so any hint that the agency could lower that rating easily unsettles financial markets.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Cyril Ramaphosa\uc2 , who replaced scandal-plagued \uc2 Jacob Zuma\uc2  as head of state in February, has staked his reputation on boosting growth and wooing foreign investors after a decade of economic stagnation.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the rand was also hurt by a resurgent U.S. dollar, which struck a 13-month peak earlier in the day, and by comments from a top official in South Africa's ruling \uc2 African National Congress (ANC) \uc2 about expropriating land from white farmers.\par \par \uc2 At 1516 GMT, the rand was 2.56 percent weaker at 14.6125 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 It is down more than 8 percent in the past week after being rattled by turmoil on Turkish financial markets, which triggered a broad emerging market sell-off.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rand.\par \par \uc2 "The only time we get involved in exchange rate markets is when there is dislocation in markets and we are far from a dislocation in financial markets," Governor \uc2 Lesetja Kganyago\uc2  told reporters in Cape Town.\par \par \uc2 In a presentation to parliament, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said economic recovery would be "weak and choppy".\par \par \uc2 Retail sales growth slowed in June, raising the possibility of a recession in the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 South African government bonds were also weaker, with the yield on the benchmark bond maturing in 2026 ending 7.5 basis points higher at 9.02 percent.\par \par \uc2 Dollar-denominated bonds issued by the South African government also fell across the curve on Wednesday after \uc2 Moody's\uc2  warning.\par \par \uc2 "We expect a slower pace of fiscal consolidation than the government of South Africa is forecasting," Lucie Villa, a Moody's vice president, said in the ratings agency's report, adding economic growth this year was expected to be lower than the government's estimates.\par \par \uc2 "It's mainly the \uc2 Moody's\uc2  comments which have sent the rand weaker," said Jan Sluis-Cremer, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at \uc2 Rand Merchant Bank\uc2 . "(ANC Chairman Gwede) Mantashe's comments on land could also be having an impact."\par \par \uc2 Mantashe said in an interview published on the News24 website that white farmers who own more than 12,000 hectares of farmland should hand over the rest to the state without compensation.\par \par \uc2 STOCKS DOWN\par \par \uc2 Stocks also fell sharply, sending the benchmark index down more than 3 percent and booking its biggest one-day percentage drop in more than two years.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 JSE\uc2  Top-40 index lost 3.76 percent to 49,615, the biggest one-day fall since June 2016. The broader All-share index was off 3.4 percent at 55,646.\par \par \uc2 Naspers\uc2 , the country biggest company by value, took the most points off index, skidding 8.2 percent as its Chinese money spinner Tencent posted its first profit fall in nearly 13 years. \uc2 Naspers\uc2  owns a 31 pct stake in Tencent.\par \par \uc2 Other decliners were mobile phone operators Vodacom, down 3.5 percent 123.57 rand, and rival \uc2 MTN Group\uc2  , which was down 2.6 percent at 99.41 rand, a level last seen eight years ago. (Additional reporting by Wendell Roelf in Cape Town and Tiisetso Motsoeneng in Johannesburg Editing by James Macharia and Richard Balmforth) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-8-15T16:29:04.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180815ee8f01uqt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
