\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 South Africa \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  "nowhere near"  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  on rand - deputy governor\b0\par\par\uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2018\par 17:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Replaces 'where' with 'were' in para 1)\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised by magnitude of rand decline\par \par \uc2 * C.bank could become involved if "market was in jeopardy"\par \par \uc2 * Could adjust policy rate if situation deteriorates\par \par \uc2 By Olivia Kumwenda-Mtambo\par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, Aug 13 (Reuters) - The \uc2 South African Reserve Bank\uc2  was surprised by the magnitude of the rand's weakness early on Monday but \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market conditions were "nowhere near" requiring the bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , deputy governor Daniel Mminele told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The rand slid more than 10 percent to a 2-year low against the dollar in early trade as a renewed rout in the Turkish lira spread to other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The turbulent unit recouped much of its losses to trade 1.23 percent weaker at 14.2525 as at 1441 GMT.\par \par \uc2 "We certainly were surprised by the magnitude of those moves," Mminele told Reuters, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets with the view to influence the exchange rate towards a particular level.\par \par \uc2 "If there were to be a situation where we were concerned that there would be huge disruptions in the market to a point where the orderly functioning of the market was in jeopardy, we would consider becoming involved but we are nowhere near those kind of circumstances," he said.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's lira has lost more than 40 percent of its value this year on worries over Turkish President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 's increasing control over the economy and deteriorating relations with the United States.\par \par \uc2 The lira did find a sliver of support when \uc2 Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had lowered reserve requirement ratios for banks. It also said it would take all necessary measures to maintain financial stability.\par \par \uc2 For South Africa, Mminele said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would monitor "the situation carefully" and look at what the movements in the rand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if sustained over time, suggested for the inflation outlook.\par \par \uc2 "If the outlook deteriorates, it may become necessary to adjust monetary policy in the future to ensure that inflation remains comfortably inside the target range and that we keep inflation expectations anchored," he said.\par \par \uc2 "It is important that one does not overreact to those short term market movements."\par \par \uc2 South Africa's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflation target range is 3 to 6 percent. The bank held its benchmark interest rate steady at 6.5 percent in July. The next interest rates decision is due on Sept. 20. (Editing by James Macharia and William Maclean) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-8-13T16:20:44.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180813ee8d02pj5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
