ar              \par  \par  NIGERIA MARKETS\par  Nigeria's share index fell to its lowest point since July\par  2012 on Monday, down 4.1 percent on the day with fund\par  managers jittery over the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's inability to\par  provide dollars for investors exiting the market.\par              \par  \par  NIGERIA CORRUPTION\par  Fifty-five people who were government ministers, state\par  governors, public officials, bankers and businessmen stole\par  1.34 trillion naira ($6.8 billion) from Nigeria's public\par  purse over a seven-year period, the information minister\par  said on Monday.\par                \par  \par  NIGERIA BUDGET\par  Nigerian President Muhammadu Buhari has written to\par  parliament requesting the withdrawal of the 2016 budget in\par  order to make changes, sources at the presidency and Senate\par  said on Sunday.\par                   \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  The Kenyan shilling KES= was unchanged against the dollar on\par  Monday, with traders saying activity was likely to remain\par  subdued until the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sets its key lending rate on\par  Wednesday. Shares fell.\par              \par  \par  KENYA TOURISM\par  Kenya's tourism sector will take another two years to\par  recover after the government beefed up security and boosted\par  funding for the sector, a key source of hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  revenues, new tourism minister Najib Balala told Reuters.\par              \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-1-19T06:16:18.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160119ec1j0060r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichg