\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Emerging central banks step in to curb  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  falls\b0\par\par\uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2015\par 12:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates throughout with latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves)\par \par \uc2 By Sujata Rao\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 2 (Reuters) - Central bankers across emerging markets are being forced into action to stem falls in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially after China allowed its yuan to weaken to four-year lows.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  index tracking 22 emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has hit successive record lows this year.\par \par \uc2 This poses a dilemma for central banks which until recently were relatively sanguine about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness due to sluggish growth and shrinking exports. But most also want to prevent excessive falls that exacerbate capital flight and inflation.\par \par \uc2 The following is a list of measures emerging central banks are taking or debating in order to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness:\par \par \uc2 TURKEY - on Aug 29 raised reserve requirements on banks' short term \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowing, upped limits on lenders transactions with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and raised interest rates on banks' lira deposits. Earlier it had said it could increase daily dollar auctions by as much as $70 million above the pre-announced minimum.\par \par \uc2 CHINA - will tighten rules on trading \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards from October to curb speculation and volatility, sources said on Sept 1. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise the yuan since a shock Aug. 11 devaluation.\par \par \uc2 CHILE - has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but on Sept. 1 the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signalled an interest rate rise by end-2015 to ward off inflation caused by the peso's fall to 12-year lows.\par \par \uc2 SOUTH KOREA - has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on and off to steady the won . Finance Minister Choi Kyung-hwan said on Aug 20 that he was looking into possible responses should risks from the yuan devaluation increase.\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA - has changed auction mechanisms of several monetary instruments and offered longer tenors to absorb banks' short-term liquidity and support the rupiah. It kept interest rates steady on Aug. 19 despite growth at six-year lows, citing the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had been "desperately defending" the rupiah, which has plumbed 17-year lows versus the dollar.\par \par \uc2 MALAYSIA - Reserves have fallen to near six-year lows after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The ringgit is at its lowest since before the government put a "floor" under it during the 1998 crisis. Prime Minister \uc2 Najib Razak\uc2  has pledged not to peg the ringgit or implement capital controls.\par \par \uc2 PERU - has tightened reserve requirements on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives after the sol hit its weakest level in nine years against the dollar. It regularly sells dollars\par \par \uc2 MEXICO - has raised daily dollar auction amounts, offering $200 million when the peso slumps more than 1 percent from the previous day's fix and another $200 million without a minimum price trigger. Governor \uc2 Agustin Carstens\uc2  said on Aug 28 a rate hike was probable within days of a Fed move.\par \par \uc2 NIGERIA - sells dollars twice weekly to bureaux de change, raising the naira off record lows on parallel markets. Banks must also pay for dollar purchases 48 hours in advance and curbed access to the interbank market to preserve foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 UGANDA - raised rates by 150 basis points to 16 percent on Aug. 10, citing inflation risks caused by shilling depreciation . Rates have risen 500 bps since April.\par \par \uc2 KENYA - has been mopping up shillings from money markets, making it expensive to hold dollars. It has raised interest rates by a total of 300 basis points since June but defied expectations of a 50-bps hike this month.\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL - has stepped up the pace of rolling over \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps aimed at supporting the real, currently at 12-year lows. 1. A source said the government would consider selling dollars through repurchase agreements before dipping into foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA - Economy Minister Alexei Ulyukayev said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could pause cutting interest rates at its next monetary policy meeting. The bank has stopped dollar purchases to reduce pressure on the rouble\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SOUTH AFRICA\b0 \highlight\uc2  - will consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to ensure "orderly market conditions", the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said after the rand plumbed record lows\par \par \uc2 SERBIA - \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Aug 24 to stem dinar losses, selling euros for the first time since April. (Reporting by Sujata Rao; Editing by Toby Chopra)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-5T10:55:21.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150902eb9200dw2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
