\par\par \b \uc2 S.Africa's rand firms after cbank says could act to curb volatility\b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2015\par 08:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, Aug 25 (Reuters) - The rand pulled back from record lows against the dollar on Tuesday after \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange markets to ease excessive volatility.               \par \par \uc2 By 0600 GMT, the rand rose 0.11 percent versus the greenback to 13.1800 after spiralling to its weakest-ever level beyond 14.00 as concerns over China's economy deepened and wreaked havoc in emerging assets.               \par \par \uc2 The absence of a new stabilisation plan from Beijing triggered panic selling on Monday across emerging markets, nudging the rand into free fall and prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to release a statement outlining its concerns about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 While not spelling out the nature of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  it was considering, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said excessive rand volatility was a concern and could warrant action.               \par \par \uc2 "This statement was mainly aimed at telling markets it will not allow the S.A. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to go into free fall," analysts at NKC African Economics said in a note. "Though tools to its disposal will tarnish its reputation of credibility."               \par \par \uc2 The bank may consider using its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to stem the sell-off, but analysts say it does not have enough to make an impact, while raising rates too sharply would hurt already weak economic growth.               \par \par \uc2 The key part of the bank's statement was that it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  "in the event of developments that threaten the orderly functioning of markets," John Cairns, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 Rand Merchant Bank\uc2  said.               \par \par \uc2 Yields were flat in early trade after rising sharply in the previous session. The benchmark 2026 issue was at 8.555 percent in early trade.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-8-25T07:57:05.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150825eb8p0079y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
