\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 South Africa \highlight\uc2  rand hits record low,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  mulls  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 2015\par 18:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Rand slips to all-time low of 14               \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Stocks, bonds not spared from sell-off   (Recasts lead with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments)               \par \par \uc2 By Mfuneko Toyana               \par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, Aug 24 (Reuters) - South Africa's rand hit an all-time low and stocks fell sharply on Monday, as rising concerns about waning growth in China hit commodity-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to say it may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to quell volatility.               \par \par \uc2 The weaker rand is likely to fuel inflation, putting pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise domestic rates further despite an economy struggling to grow in the face of South Africa's worst power crisis in seven years.               \par \par \uc2 The rand recorded its biggest daily loss in 19 months, touching 14 to the dollar, its weakest level on record according to Thomson Reuters data. By 1545 GMT it was trading at 13.2, down 1.81 percent from Friday's close.               \par \par \uc2 The benchmark top-40 share index closed about 3 percent lower, in a broad-based decline.               \par \par \uc2 Government bonds were not spared the sell-off, with the yield for the 2026 benchmark pushed to its highest in more than two months, reinforcing the case for a further interest rate rise this year.               \par \par \uc2 While not spelling out the nature of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  it was considering, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said excessive rand volatility was a concern and could warrant action.               \par \par \uc2 Ricardo da Camara, an economist at ETM Analytics said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not have enough foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to stem the sell-off nor could it raise rates at this stage.               \par \par \uc2 "If the market really wants to sell the rand it is going to do so. So the SARB (\uc2 South African Reserve Bank\uc2 ) would really be wasting their reserves trying to fight the markets," he said.               \par \par \uc2 "A simple 25 basis point hike in these conditions won't necessarily do anything. It would have to be more pronounced, 50, 75 or even 100 basis points, but that would just kill growth," da Camara said.               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the benchmark repo rate by 25 basis points to 6 percent in July, the first increase in a year, on signs inflation is steadily edging towards the top end of a 3-6 percent target band.               \par \par \uc2 The rand was among the weakest of 25 emerging market peers as investors sold off high-risk assets amid worries about the impact of slowing global growth in the world's No. 2 economy.               \par \par \uc2 Chinese stocks plunged more than 8 percent on Monday, a tumble rooted in investor disappointment that Beijing did not announce expected policy support over the weekend after China's main market indexes shed 11 percent last week.               \par \par \uc2 The rand, which is down more than 15 percent against the dollar this year, has been particularly vulnerable because of South Africa's weak fundamentals, including a wide current account balance and sluggish growth.               \par \par \uc2 Charts showed that the rand had broken through the top of its four-year upward sloping channel trend line.               \par \par \uc2 "A close above 13.50, being the top channel line level, on a weekly basis would ensure further woes for the rand over the next couple of weeks/months," \uc2 Standard Bank\uc2  trader Warrick Butler said.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-8-24T17:56:03.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150824eb8o006ej\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
