\par\par \b \uc2 African Markets - Factors to watch on Jan 23\b0\par\par\uc2 497 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2015\par 06:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par moves and political events may affect African markets on Friday.\par     - - - - -\par  EVENTS:\par  GHANA - Expecting the latest Producer Price Index data.\par  \par  GLOBAL MARKETS\par  Asian stocks extended a global rally on Friday after the\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  launched a landmark bond-buying\par  stimulus programme that buoyed investors' risk appetite,\par  drove bonds higher and left the euro pinned near 11-year\par  lows.\par             \par  \par  WORLD OIL PRICES\par  Oil prices jumped in Asian trading on Friday as news of the\par  death of Saudi Arabia's King Abdullah added to uncertainty\par  in energy markets already facing some of the biggest shifts\par  in decades.\par       \par  \par  EMERGING MARKETS\par  For the top emerging markets news, double click on\par             \par  \par  AFRICA STOCKS\par  For the latest news on African stocks, click on     \par  \par  AFRICAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  Nigeria's naira is expected to lose more ground next week,\par  hit by the slide in crude prices and a decline in dollar\par  liquidity, while other African \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are likely to\par  remain on the back foot unless their respective central\par  banks \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par                 \par  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SOUTH AFRICA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKETS\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Africa\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rand powered to its firmest in nearly 18\par  months against the euro on Thursday and notched up a 6-week\par  high against the dollar after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  unveiled a 60 billion euro-a-month asset purchase programme\par  to boost growth.\par                 \par  \par  NIGERIA MARKETS\par  Nigeria's naira          recovered from record lows hit this\par  week after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  increased \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading limits\par  and sold dollars to commercial lenders on Thursday, dealers\par  said.\par                 \par  \par  NIGERIA ELECTION\par  Nigeria should delay next month's elections to give\par  organisers more time to distribute millions of biometric ID\par  cards to voters, the country's top security official said on\par  Thursday.\par                 \par  \par  NIGERIA INSURGENCY\par  Nigeria's campaign against Islamist \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boko Haram\f28 \uc2 \f2  insurgents is\par  being hampered by "cowards" in its armed forces, its\par  presidential security adviser said in a rare public sign of\par  high-level unhappiness with the effort.\par                 \par  \par  KENYA MARKETS\par  The Kenyan shilling        edged down against the dollar on\par  Thursday, though traders said they saw signs of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  strengthening in the coming days with more dollars coming\par  into the market. Stocks were up.\par                 \par  \par  KENYA TREASURIES\par  The average weighted yield on Kenya's 91-day Treasury bill\par             rose to 8.684 percent at auction on Thursday from\par  8.601 percent last week, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said.\par                 \par  \par  ZAMBIA ELECTION\par  Zambia's ruling party presidential candidate Edgar Lungu\par  took a slim lead over his rival Hakainde Hichilema after\par  votes from more than half of constituencies were counted,\par  the electoral commission said on Thursday.\par                 \par  \par  UGANDA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 Uganda's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday sold an undisclosed amount\par  of dollars for a fifth time this month to slow the\par  shilling's depreciation after the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came under\par  pressure from heavy dollar demand.\par                 \par  \par      For the latest precious metals report click on        \par      For the latest base metals report click on         \par      For the latest crude oil report click on\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-1-23T06:31:53.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150123eb1n004xz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
