\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chinese stocks shift to reverse, falling oil hits rouble\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chris Vellacott   \par \uc2 522 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2014\par 11:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 9 (Reuters) - Chinese stocks fell hard on Tuesday, posting their biggest one-day fall since the financial crisis as gloom pervading emerging markets hit the world's second largest economy.\par \par \uc2 Sentiment towards emerging markets has taken a knock in recent months from a rising U.S. dollar which has lured speculative money away while assets in energy exporters such as Russia and Nigeria have taken a knock from a falling oil price.\par \par \uc2 China's Shanghai Composite Index was down 5.3 percent at the close of trading, the biggest single-day percentage drop since 2009.\par \par \uc2 The reversal has dented a stock market boom in China led by retail investors betting on more monetary stimulus from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up growth who recently sent Shanghai shares to multi-year highs.\par \par \uc2 Much of the day's setback is attributed by analysts to profit taking, though weak Chinese trade data and a regulatory ruling forbidding local bonds rated AA or below from being pledged as collateral for stock purchases also damaged the mood.\par \par \uc2 "The market has been over-valued for some time and people were waiting for some news to sell and this was the trigger. This bull market has been going on since around 2009 and I'm not sure it has run its course yet as there may be some more upside to come," said Per Hammarlund, chief emerging markets strategist at SEB in Stockholm.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the impact of a falling oil price rattled assets in energy exporting countries, driving Russian stocks lower with the dollar-denominated RTS index falling 1.8 percent having earlier reached a five-year low.\par \par \uc2 The rouble was 0.9 percent weaker against the dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it spent $1.9 billion defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Friday, bringing \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the week to $4.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 Another oil \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nigeria's naira, shed 1.9 percent against the dollar in spite of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rand recovered its pose, rising 0.5 percent on the dollar to reverse some of the losses from the previous session that saw it tumble to a multi-year low, depressed by the prospect of weakening global demand for its commodities.\par \par \uc2 South Africa is among the emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen as most vulnerable to the impact of a rising dollar.\par \par \uc2 Turkey's lira, also sensitive to a strong dollar, rose 0.3 percent on Tuesday, adding to the previous session's gains on the back of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doubling the size of its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction.\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance 2014, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jus35t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jus35t}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging index performance 2014, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/weh36s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/weh36s}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging Europe performance 2014, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jun28s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jun28s}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on MSCI frontier index performance 2014, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/zyh97s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/zyh97s}}}\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see ) (Editing by Janet Lawrence) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-9T11:14:15.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141209eac9009jg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
