\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 South Africa central bank \highlight\uc2  says unlikely to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to stabilise the rand\b0\par\par\uc2 373 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2014\par 19:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds more details)\par \par \uc2 By Xola Potelwa\par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, April 8 (Reuters) - \uc2 South Africa's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects the rand to remain volatile although it is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to try and stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Governor \uc2 Gill Marcus\uc2  said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "We have not attempted to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as we do not believe that such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be effective," Marcus said in a speech given at the European Economics and Financial Centre in London and posted on the bank's website.\par \par \uc2 South Africa has reserves of only about $50 billion, giving it limited firepower to shore up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and Marcus has previously said the bank would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rand has touched five-year lows this year as emerging markets, which benefited from easy monetary policy in developed markets, took a knock as the United States started to scale back monetary stimulus and as investors fretted about South Africa's wide current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since recouped some losses after the Reserve Bank unexpectedly raised interest rates in January for the first time in nearly six years, and was trading at its strongest level this year against the dollar on Tuesday. .\par \par \uc2 The bank has said the rate hike was the start of a moderate monetary tightening cycle. It held rates steady at its last meeting in March but is widely expected to increase lending rates again at its next meeting in May.\par \par \uc2 Marcus said on Tuesday that despite challenges in the platinum mines, where strikes have stopped production for the last 10 weeks, she was optimistic about an improvement in the current account.\par \par \uc2 "So despite the ongoing challenges to platinum exports, we are cautiously optimistic that we may be seeing a sustained improvement in the current account."\par \par \uc2 The current account deficit narrowed at the end of last year to 5.1 percent of gross domestic product, but analysts said it was the wrong kind of rebalancing as imports contracted due to a lack of demand, a further sign that the economy is struggling. (Additional reporting by Olivia Kumwenda-Mtambo; Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-4-11T17:31:34.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140408ea4800rs5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
