\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: Manufacturing a Drag on South Africa GDP\b0\par\par\uc2 By Patrick McGroarty And Devon Maylie   \par \uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2013\par 19:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 PRETORIA--Grim economic figures released Tuesday sent South Africa's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a four-year low, as officials searched for ways to boost the continent's biggest economy.\par \par \uc2 The rand fell to ZAR9.80 to the U.S. dollar, its weakest position since March 2009, after South Africa's statistics agency said a marginal recovery at the country's strike-hit mines wasn't enough to offset a steep drop in manufacturing activity in the first quarter.\par \par \uc2 South Africa's economy expanded only 1.9% annually in the first three months of this year, the agency said, falling short of the 2.2% growth that many economists had forecast, according to Absa Capital, a South African subsidiary of \uc2 Barclays PLC\uc2 . The weaker-than-expected growth will make it difficult for South Africa to meet its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forecast of 2.4% growth for 2013, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced last week from 2.7%.\par \par \uc2 South Africa's slowing growth and wobbly \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sparked concerns in the government because even-tougher times may still be ahead. Workers across industries including mines and automobiles, are threatening to strike over wage increases and power constraints could cut into factory production.\par \par \uc2 In the past week, South Africa's president, finance minister and top central banker each acknowledged the nation's darkening economic prospects, and urged workers and employers to end a vicious cycle of unauthorized strikes and pay-raise demands well beyond South Africa's 5.9% inflation rate.\par \par \uc2 But they have had little luck quelling those forces so far. Wildcat strikes that have caused work stoppages at chrome and platinum mines have surfaced regularly since police shot and killed 34 miners outside Johannesburg last August.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Finance Minister Pravin Gordhan and Mineral Resources Minister Susan Shabangu met on Friday with mining executives and agreed to spend the next month discussing ways to avoid further strikes and protect jobs and profit.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Ms. Shabangu told \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's parliament she was planning "supply and demand side \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 " into the platinum and gold sectors that make up the bulk of the country's mining output. She didn't explain what those \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  might entail, but unions said she has urged companies and unions to avoid layoffs at all costs.\par \par \uc2 "I have directed my officials to urgently...develop a rescue plan, which will enable us to find appropriate governmentwide measures," Ms. Shabangu said.\par \par \uc2 South Africa's official unemployment rate is 25.2%, and Reserve Bank Governor Gill Marcus said last week that it could climb if labor strife and lackluster growth persisted.\par \par \uc2 Although the rand is down nearly 15% against the dollar since the start of the year, manufacturers haven't managed to sell more of their relatively cheaper goods abroad, the data released on Tuesday showed.\par \par \uc2 "A cocktail of high domestic costs, supply constraints and low global demand are still holding the sector back," said Coenraad Bezuidenhout, executive director of the Manufacturing Circle industry group.\par \par \uc2 A large steelworkers' union has said it would demand a 20% pay rise for 50,000 car- and tire-factory workers in coming wage talks. Also, South Africa's state-backed utility Eskom said coming maintenance work could reduce its capacity to generate electricity by as much as 25% during the looming southern hemisphere winter.\par \par \uc2 Write to Patrick McGroarty at patrick.mcgroarty@dowjones.com and Devon Maylie at devon.maylie@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 28, 2013 13:18 ET (17:18 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130528e95s003zf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
