\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Stocks hit 2013 lows as Cyprus debacle weighs\b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 11:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 20 (Reuters) - Emerging stocks hit their lowest point so far this year on Wednesday as Cyprus's financial debacle dented demand for risky assets, while the rand was steady after South Africa kept interest rates on hold.\par \par \uc2 Cyprus's parliament overwhelmingly rejected on Tuesday a European bailout that included a levy on all bank deposits, and Russia and Cyprus failed to agree on a loan deal on Wednesday, ramping up the chances of the island defaulting.\par \par \uc2 "This Cyprus thing has shaken up everything," said \uc2 Lars Christensen\uc2 , chief emerging markets analyst at \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "For the first time in five years we had some kind of real stability in the market, and this has wrecked everything."\par \par \uc2 Benchmark emerging equities hit their lowest since early December before trimming losses. They have fallen nearly 3 percent this year.\par \par \uc2 Emerging markets continue to get some support, however, from money-printing in the developed world, which is driving funds towards higher-yielding assets.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  is expected to stick with quantitative easing when it makes its interest rate decision later on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "We have support from policies from Japan and the Fed, and that's curbing some of the rise in risk aversion," Christensen said.\par \par \uc2 Chinese stocks were also buoyant, enjoying their best day in more than two months.\par \par \uc2 The crisis in Cyprus has stoked unease about emerging economies inclined to unconventional policy measures, such as Hungary.\par \par \uc2 The cost of insuring Hungary's debt against default rose to five-month highs at 347 basis points in the five-year credit default swap market, according to Markit.\par \par \uc2 Hungarian stocks recovered from 2-1/2 month lows, however, and the forint pulled off recent 14-month lows, helped by verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past week.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rand was steady above recent four-year lows after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left rates unchanged as expected. Weak growth has weighed on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor \uc2 Gill Marcus\uc2  said its depreciation was somewhat overdone.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Carolyn Cohn and Sujata Rao; Editing by Hugh Lawson)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING | ABN | M | D | E | RBN | SF | AFN | HX | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130323e93k0004y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
