\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  GLOBAL CALL: Our Take on the Day's Big  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  News\b0\par\par\uc2 458 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 12:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Global Call covers the main talking points from a news meeting involving DJ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trader editors in New York, London and Singapore, as well as other \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  hot spots when warranted.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     By Brian Baskin \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1. The South African rand's slide is picking up speed, rising above 9.19 to the dollar--its weakest since April 2009--after the country's current account deficit narrowed by less than expected in the fourth quarter. The weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped tighten the deficit by boosting exports and making imports more expensive. But gold exports were hit by strikes, a problem that has continued into 2013. The question investors face now is how far they can push the rand before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  feels compelled to step in. \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  less than many other emerging markets, but won't stay on the sidelines forever. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets next week to set interest rates, and may tip its hand then.\par \par \uc2 2. The U.K. pound hit its lowest point against the dollar since June 2010 after industrial production fell in January, raising fears of a triple-dip recession. The damage looks even uglier against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the sterling at its weakest against the Australian dollar since 1985. The market is bracing for easing from the Bank of England, which becomes more likely the worse the economic indicators get.\par \par \uc2 3. Spanish bond yields are slightly lower after a successful short-term debt auction, where it sold more than expected. The 10-year bond is at 4.74%, just above Italy's 4.64%. It may only be a matter of time before they cross, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 4. The yen hit another high against the dollar, trading up to 96.71 after the nominee for Bank of Japan governor told lawmakers that "a sense of speed is important" and that every option must be taken to pull out of deflation. A nominee for Bank of Japan deputy governor also called for more asset purchases to meet a 2% inflation goal. It was yet another reminder that Prime Minister Shinzo Abe is installing aggressive advocates for loose monetary policy at the BOJ.\par \par \uc2 5. Asian markets were hit by new concerns that China's new government will adopt tighter monetary policy. In addition to recent controls on the property market, the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  is withdrawing liquidity from the market via repurchasing agreements, including 26 billion yuan ($4.18 billion) on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 (Brian Baskin is assistant managing editor for the Americas at DJ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trader, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  news service jointly produced by Dow Jones Newswires and The Wall Street Journal.) [ 12-03-13 1128GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020130312e93c0000u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
