\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 , Debt Buoyed As Dollar Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 605 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 2012\par 22:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt mostly had a strong run Wednesday as talk of more quantitative easing pushed the dollar weaker.\par \par \uc2 The day was full of big headlines that moved markets during various continental trading hours. \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  change of India's sovereign outlook to negative sharply weakened the Indian rupee during the day. Then, the European Commission opened the doors for Hungary to begin negotiations with the European Union and International Monetary Fund, leading to the forint hitting a nine-week high against the euro.\par \par \uc2 During the New York afternoon, the Federal Reserve's Open Market Committee indicated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could pump more liquidity into the system. This turned into a dollar negative, and led to further appreciation of emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar's weakness reverses days of ambivalent trading that was characterized by modest volumes and investors' reluctance to make any strong bets.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the Hungarian forint was the leader on the board, as it appreciated nearly 2% against both the dollar and the euro. Investors and analysts cautioned against reading too much into the Hungarian government's actions, calling it the first step in a long process of securing backup support for Hungary's debt burden.\par \par \uc2 Still, investors and hedge funds rushed to cover their shorts on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leading to strong demand and a rapid firming up of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Risk premiums on Hungary's sovereign debt tightened by more than 48 basis points to 552 basis points over comparable Treasury yields.\par \par \uc2 In the New York afternoon, Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke reiterated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "entirely prepared" to embark on actions and programs to support the U.S. economy. Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged as another round of quantitative easing would trigger a fresh round of buying of these higher-yielding assets by investors.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was at ZAR7.7484 against the South African rand, down 0.63% on the day, and back to levels at the start of this month.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, the dollar was at TRL1.7692 against the Turkish lira, down 0.65% on the day, and back to levels at the start of March.\par \par \uc2 Brazil remained the outlier, with the dollar strengthening against the real after \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central government. The dollar was trading at BRL1.8819, a tad stronger than its Tuesday close of BRL1.8793.\par \par \uc2 Also, if the Fed adopts another round of quantitative easing, then more central banks may follow Brazil's lead in making moves to curb local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength. Already, most of these countries blame the rounds of easing in the developed world for their appreciating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and surges in speculative capital flows to their local markets. Brazil, the most aggressive of all, has initiated a range of taxes and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to depreciate its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Other central banks, from South Korea to Peru, are constantly in the market, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower the volatility of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  is calling for coordinated capital control, and its finance minister said this topic dominated chats at the recent IMF meetings.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, emerging-market sovereign debt was stronger, with risk premiums five basis points tighter to 351 basis points over comparable Treasury yields. Risk premiums on Argentina's debt narrowed more than 27 basis points to 977 basis points, as the sovereign debt, which is vulnerable to strong swings in investor sentiment, benefited from the broad market sentiment.\par \par \uc2 -By Prabha Natarajan, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2468; prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com @djfxtrader [ 25-04-12 2035GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120425e84p001fc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
