\par\par \b \uc2 S.Africa's ANC mulls wider  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  mandate - paper\b0\par\par\uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 15:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * ANC contemplates constitutional changes - report\par \par \uc2 * Reserve bank mandate "narrow," may require review\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Reserve Bank\uc2  should weaken rand exchange rate\par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, March 4 (Reuters) - The ruling African National Congress (ANC) is mulling reforms to South Africa's constitution which would include changing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's powers and price stability mandate, a local paper reported on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 City Press newspaper quoted the ANC as saying elements of the constitution that may require review included the "narrow mandate of the \uc2 Reserve Bank\uc2  or the relationship between and powers of the different spheres of government".\par \par \uc2 The government set the bank's monetary policy goal as containing inflation, which the bank does with a flexible inflation targeting strategy, aiming for a 3 to 6 percent inflation rate since 2000.\par \par \uc2 The South African Reserve Bank is perceived to be independent of government even as it regularly consults with the finance ministry. Its ultimate accountability is to parliament.\par \par \uc2 Inflation breached the bank's target in November and stood at 6.3 percent in January partly on the rising cost of imports into South Africa.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank\uc2  sees inflation returning back within the band only in the first quarter of 2013.\par \par \uc2 A strong rand shields the country from some inflation pressure, however unions bemoan the exchange rate, urging the \uc2 Reserve Bank\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and make \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exports more competitive.\par \par \uc2 NOT ENOUGH FIREPOWER\par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank Governor Gill Marcus has continually said the bank does not target a level of the rand and buys foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to build up its reserves. The bank previously had an exchange-rate targeting mandate.\par \par \uc2 Its reserves, at about $49 billion in January, would not provide the bank with enough firepower to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets regularly.\par \par \uc2 The paper said some members of the ANC were calling for the inflation targeting strategy to be scrapped.\par \par \uc2 A senior official at the department of trade and industry criticised the \uc2 Reserve Bank\uc2  for not taking action against the "overvalued" rand, saying other \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's manage their exchange rates while South Africa was following an old inflation targeting view.\par \par \uc2 "This is a wrong policy, you have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it becomes too strong," Lionel October, director-general at the department, said.\par \par \uc2 The rand closed weaker at 7.54 against the dollar on Friday but is seen strengthening in the short term as a long term liquidity injection from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds carry trades.\par \par \uc2 The ANC, which holds a policy-setting conference in June, will release draft policy discussion documents to its branches on Monday. Proposals in the discussion papers would have to be adopted at another conference in December to shape government policy.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Xola Potelwa; Editing by David Holmes)\par \par \uc2 SAFRICA-ANC/CBANK | AFN | ABN | D | M | SF | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120304e8340006v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
