\par\par \b \uc2 South African Markets - Factors to watch on May 5\b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2011\par 07:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, May 5 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves and political events may affect South African markets on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 DIARY\par \par \uc2 For South Africa corporate diary, click on [ZA/EQUITY]\par \par \uc2 For southern and South Africa diary, click on [ZA/DIARY]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH AFRICAN \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government is not planning to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the rand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has helped to cushion the impact of higher oil and food prices, Finance Minister Pravin Gordhan said on Wednesday. [ID:nLDE74306D]\par \par \uc2 MASSMART\par \par \uc2 South Africa wants "concrete commitments" from U.S. retail giant \uc2 Wal-Mart\uc2  not to cut jobs in its proposed takeover of regional chain Massmart , trade minister Rob Davies said on Wednesday. [ID:nLDE743293]\par \par \uc2 BRAIT\par \par \uc2 Shareholders of the private equity group have approved the 5.9 billion rand rights offer at a meeting on Wednesday, Brait said. [ID:nWEA8666]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH AFRICAN UNIONS\par \par \uc2 South Africa's National Union of Metal Workers (NUMSA) said on Wednesday it wanted a 20 percent, one-year wage increase for all employees from South Africa's steel and engineering body. [ID:nLDE74323B]\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS\par \par \uc2 Silver nursed losses on Thursday after suffering its biggest three-day drop in five years on heavy profit taking while the euro consolidated gains against the dollar before the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting where it is expected to reinforce its hawkish outlook. [MKTS/GLOB]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH AFRICAN MARKETS\par \par \uc2 South Africa's rand weakened against the dollar on Wednesday as importers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar buying kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its perceived stronger bias while government bonds were nearly unchanged in a quiet session. [.J] [ZAR/]\par \par \uc2 PRECIOUS METALS\par \par \uc2 Gold held steady, with traders hesitant to take positions before the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate decision due later in the day. [GOL/]\par \par \uc2 WALL STREET\par \par \uc2 Weak economic figures heightened stock investors' anxiety over the extended rally, knocking U.S. shares lower for a third day on Wednesday. [.N]\par \par \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS\par \par \uc2 For the top emerging markets news, double click on [nTOPEMRG]\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 Some of the main stories out of the South African press:\par \par \uc2 BUSINESS DAY\par \par \uc2 - Zuma seeks "fair deal" in Africa's ties with China\par \par \uc2 - Aquarius puts up 1.2 billion rand in Northam deal\par \par \uc2 - Standard Bank strategy "seeks to pacify shareholders"\par \par \uc2 BUSINESS REPORT\par \par \uc2 - "Africa fails to train right skills"\par \par \uc2 - Altron in shopping mood after double-digit profit\par \par \uc2 (Compiled by Tiisetso Motsoeneng)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SAFRICA-FACTORS/   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110508e75500039\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
