\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Gordhan says S.Africa not planning rand  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 586 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2011\par 17:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rand gains have helped with inflation\par \par \uc2 * Govt still concerned about capital inflows\par \par \uc2 * Trade Minister says rand overvalued\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background)\par \par \uc2 CAPE TOWN, May 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government is not planning to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the rand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has helped to cushion the impact of higher oil and food prices, Finance Minister Pravin Gordhan said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The government's rand policy is a touchy issue between the ruling African National Congress and its leftist allies who would rather see the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened and Gordhan's comments could add to ongoing tensions in the alliance over policy.\par \par \uc2 The rand has gained more than 30 percent against the dollar since the beginning of 2009. It hit its strongest levels in more than three years this week and was last trading at 6.64.\par \par \uc2 "At this stage we are not planning on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Gordhan said on the sidelines of the World Economic Forum (WEF).\par \par \uc2 Gordhan told SABC TV earlier on Wednesday that it was fortunate that the biggest economy in Africa was experiencing a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , adding had it not been for the rand's gains, fuel and food prices would be much higher.\par \par \uc2 Like other emerging markets, strong capital inflows into South Africa in the wake of loose monetary policy in developed countries have been the main driver of the rand's gains.\par \par \uc2 Gordhan said the government was still concerned about the impact of short-term capital inflows. South Africa rejected the idea of implementing a tax on capital inflow, like other countries such as Brazil, but has opted to raise its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to limit rand gains.\par \par \uc2 Inflation has been within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of between 3 and 6 percent since February 2010, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects it to stay in that band until the end of 2012. It stood at 4.1 percent year-on-year in March.\par \par \uc2 South Africa's benign inflation environment has allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the repo rate steady at 5.5 percent at a time when other emerging markets are starting to tighten monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect South Africa to start raising interest rates only towards the end of the year, after decreasing them by 650 basis points between December 2008 and December 2010.\par \par \uc2 The rand's gains have hurt the manufacturing sector, Gordhan acknowledged. "It does have a negative impact on manufacturing," he said.\par \par \uc2 At current levels, it is considered too strong by manufacturers who would rather see it trading above 8.00 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The sector was the hardest hit by a recession in 2009 and although it is on a recovery, output levels are still below pre-recession levels.\par \par \uc2 Trade Minister Rob Davies, a left-leaning cabinet member, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was overvalued but did not say what \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy the government should pursue.\par \par \uc2 "The rand is overvalued due to the continued uneven nature of the world economic recovery and the policies that are being followed by some of the major players," Davies said at the WEF.\par \par \uc2 "The overvalued rand is still hitting us in the value-added sectors," he added.\par \par \uc2 With a quarter of the labour force jobless, South Africa has to balance the impact of the rand on inflation with ensuring that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not strangle key sectors such as manufacturing and constrain economic growth.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Phumza Macanda, Peroshni Govender and Ed Cropley; Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 SAFRICA-RAND/ (UPDATE 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110507e754000hl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
