\par\par \b \uc2 S.Africa's rand at one-week low vs dlr, futures down\b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2011\par 07:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rand weaker on the year due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Bonds follow \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower\par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, Feb 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rand fell to a one-week low against the dollar on Friday due to continued \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying although traders said levels of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were lower than previous weeks.\par \par \uc2 The rand has weakened 10 percent against the dollar this year as the \uc2 South African Reserve Bank\uc2  (SARB) has stepped in to try and keep it in check after a sharp appreciation in December.\par \par \uc2 At 0642 GMT the rand <ZAR=D3> traded at 7.2975 to the dollar, 0.27 percent weaker than its Thursday close of 7.2775. It briefly touched 7.30, its lowest since Feb. 4.\par \par \uc2 "For now, dollar/rand remains safely in the 7.17 to 7.30 range but risks have switched back to the upside," \uc2 Rand Merchant Bank\uc2  said in a note. The rand is one of the worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year.\par \par \uc2 "Global events have played a role, but we believe that the leading drivers of this weakening trend are South African-driven," Jeff Gable of Absa Capital said after moving his year-end forecast to 7.60 from 7.10.\par \par \uc2 "Following December's sharp appreciation it has experienced a world-leading sell-off thus far in 2011," Absa Capital said.\par \par \uc2 The easing of exchange controls for South Africans and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's "increasingly aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " were the main factors driving the weakness, Absa said.\par \par \uc2 Government bonds traded slightly lower than their closing levels on Thursday. The yield on the 2015 issue <ZAR=D3> rose 0.5 basis points to 7.865 percent and that on the 2026 paper <ZAR186=> was up by the same margin to 8.715 percent.\par \par \uc2 The JSE's blue-chip March stock futures contract <ALSIc1> fell 0.26 percent ahead of the 0700 GMT start of stock market trading. (Reporting by Xola Potelwa; Editing by Ed Cropley)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SAFRICA/MORNING|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SF|AFN|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110214e72b000la\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
