\par\par \b \uc2 S.African stocks hit by Chinese rate hike; rand firms\b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2011\par 18:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Stocks drop on China rate hike\par \par \uc2 * Rand firms up as concerns over Egypt ease\par \par \uc2 * Fourth quarter jobless rate dips\par \par \uc2 By Vuyani Ndaba and Gugulakhe Lourie\par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, Feb 8 (Reuters) - South African stocks inched lower for the second straight day on Tuesday but remained near 2-1/2-year highs, as a rate hike by China made it easier for investors to cash in shares after recent aggressive gains.\par \par \uc2 The rand firmed, however, as concerns over Egypt eased and dealers bet the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would slow the pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after weeks of aggressive dollar-buying.\par \par \uc2 The JSE Top-40 index of blue chips <.JTOPI> shed 0.02 percent to 29,616.21, while the broader All-Share index <.JALSH> was down 0.03 percent to 32,788.86.\par \par \uc2 Major losers among the Top-40 included platinum producer \uc2 Lonmin\uc2  , which dropped 2.8 percent to 208.50 rand, and consumer goods firm Tiger Brands , which fell 1.85 percent to 186 rand.\par \par \uc2 "Due to the Chinese hiking their rate, a bit of nervousness in the market (is) halting a short-term rally," said Wilmar Buys, a trader at FFO Securities.\par \par \uc2 China raised interest rates on Tuesday for the second time in just over six weeks in what is seen as an ongoing battle against high inflation. [ID:nTOE706030]\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 ArcelorMittal\uc2  South Africa closed 0.41 percent lower at 85 rand. The shares tumbled more than 4 percent in the session after the company's full-year results came in well below analyst estimates. [ID::nLDE717063]\par \par \uc2 RAND GAINS\par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts say investor concerns over Egypt have eased and the market is better absorbing the news on the political situation in the north African country.\par \par \uc2 "The market has adjusted to Egypt, and European problems are on the back burner so (investors) are looking for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that offer attractive (yields)," said Imran Ahmad, emerging market strategist at RBS.\par \par \uc2 At 1615 GMT, the rand <ZAR=D3> was trading at 7.1720 against the dollar, 0.86 percent stronger than its close of 7.2344 on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Ahmad added that the \uc2 South African Reserve Bank\uc2  might take a break from buying dollars in the market to try and stem gains on the rand.\par \par \uc2 "Perhaps (the SARB) is going to be less \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  now given the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fatigue and especially given the cost of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $44.451 billion at the end January, up more than $1 billion in a month. Analysts have said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have the firepower to continue that rate of accumulation.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the positive tone for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were unemployment figures showing the official jobless rate for the fourth quarter of 2010 edged down to 24.0 percent from 25.3 percent in the third quarter. [ID:nLDE7170TH]\par \par \uc2 The market did not react to the fall in the jobless rate but analysts say the marginal drop bodes well for the outlook on the South African economy.\par \par \uc2 Government bonds gained as the yield on the 2015 benchmark government issue <ZAR157=> fell by 3.5 basis points to 7.865 percent, while the 2026 issue <ZAR186=> went down by three basis points 8.675 percent.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SAFRICA/CLOSE|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SF|AFN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110208e728001ei\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
