\par\par \b \uc2 S.Africa rand steadies vs dlr, but lags peers\b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2011\par 07:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rand underperforms peers as foreigners dump local debt\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also weighs on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, Feb 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rand steadied against the dollar on Friday after tumbling to near six-month lows overnight, with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying and foreigners' unbundling of local debt seen keeping pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At 0642 GMT the rand <ZAR=D3> traded at 7.2710 against the dollar, little changed from Thursday's close in New York of 7.2605.\par \par \uc2 The rand fell more than 1.7 percent to 7.3001/dollar on Thursday -- pushing through its long-term moving average and reaching its weakest level since Sept. 2 last year -- with some traders citing dollar demand from offshore hedge funds.\par \par \uc2 Rand Merchant Bank\uc2  said in a research note the rand had underperformed peers since the start of this year, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Australia, New Zealand, Canada and Brazil all remaining relatively strong.\par \par \uc2 "It seems that the two most obvious factors are that foreigners have been selling bonds, and we've heard that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying dollars aggressively," RMB \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst John Cairns told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners have sold a net 9.15 billion rand of South African government bonds since the start of the year, according to data from the Johannesburg stock exchange. [ID:nLDE7101MT]\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained about 12 percent against the dollar last year, triggering concerns about the export sector, and the Reserve Bank has said it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to build up \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves whenever appropriate, a move seen capping rand strength.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark 2015 government bond <ZAR157=> extended Thursday's losses, with the yield subsequently adding four basis points to 7.96 percent. The yield on the 2026 note <ZAR186=> was unchanged from its previous closing level of 8.765 percent.\par \par \uc2 The JSE's blue-chip March stock futures contract <ALSIc1> crept up just 0.17 percent, hinting at a flat start for the local share market at 0700 GMT. (Reporting by Stella Mapenzauswa; Editing by Ed Cropley)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SAFRICA/MORNING|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|SF|AFN|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110207e724000gj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
