\par\par \b \uc2 S.Africa's rand retreats against dlr, targets 6.95\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2011\par 07:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * Importer demand seen adding pressure on rand\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb strength\par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, Jan 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rand weakened against the dollar on Tuesday after struggling to hold on to 3-1/2 year highs the previous day and should relinquish further ground as importer demand rises after the holiday break.\par \par \uc2 At 0641 GMT the rand traded at 6.67 against the greenback, 0.6 percent softer than Monday's closing level of 6.63.\par \par \uc2 The rand rallied strongly in December, traditionally a strong month for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as exporters off-load dollars for cash-flow purposes before year-end.\par \par \uc2 Importer demand should now start picking up strongly as manufacturers in particular re-open their businesses after the festive break, Standard Bank trader Warrick Butler said.\par \par \uc2 "What you might see as well is the Reserve Bank probably becoming a lot more active given how strong the rand has been. I think you're going to see a bit of a pull-back in the strength of the rand," he added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempted to stem the rand's gains in 2010 by quickening the pace of its accumulation of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 "The big level is the 6.74 area on the top side. We've struggled with 6.60 over the course of December, so I think we're due for a bit of a corrective move. Initially we're looking at 6.74/75 and from there 6.95 will be the next place to target," Butler said.\par \par \uc2 Government bonds were flat after Monday's strong gains, with the yield on the 2015 bond <ZAR157=> steady at the previous day's close of 7.275 percent and that on the 2026 note <ZAR186=> steady at 8.265 percent.\par \par \uc2 The JSE's blue chip March stock futures contract <ALSIc1> edged up just 0.17 percent, pointing to a sluggish start to trade on the local bourse at 0700 GMT. (Reporting by Stella Mapenzauswa; Editing by Ed Cropley)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SAFRICA/MORNING|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|SF|AFN|RNP|DNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110107e714000if\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
