\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-S.Africa wants weak rand to aid growth despite G20\b0\par\par\uc2 1,039 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2010\par 11:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * "Active monetary policy \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to weaken rand\par \par \uc2 * Government insists plan not in conflict with G20 pledge\par \par \uc2 * Rand up nearly 30 percent vs dollar since start of 2009\par \par \uc2 * Analysts doubt authorities can easily control \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Finance minister to discuss growth plan on Wednesday\par \par \uc2 (Adds analysis of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's position, graphic)\par \par \uc2 By Wendell Roelf and Stella Mapenzauswa\par \par \uc2 CAPE TOWN, Oct 26 (Reuters) - South Africa said on Tuesday that it would weaken its rand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost economic growth, threatening a deal to refrain from competitive devaluations reached by the Group of 20 major nations just three days ago.\par \par \uc2 The statement by South African presidency minister Collins Chabane appeared to mark a policy shift by President Jacob Zuma's government, which previously had resisted calls by labour unions to stimulate exports by weakening the rand <ZAR=D3>.\par \par \uc2 Chabane, describing a new long-term growth plan for South Africa, said it "entails a careful balancing of more active monetary policy \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to achieve growth...through a more competitive exchange rate and a lower cost of capital."\par \par \uc2 The plan sees unemployment falling to 15 percent from 25.3 percent currently over the next 10 years, implying the creation of 5 million jobs during that period, the government said.\par \par \uc2 At a meeting of G20 finance ministers and central bankers in South Korea last weekend, countries pledged to "refrain from competitive devaluations" of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As a G20 member, South Africa was party to the agreement. [ID:nTOE69M004]\par \par \uc2 A South African government spokesman insisted on Tuesday that there was no contradiction between his country's plan and the G20 pledge, which was designed to reduce the risk of a global trade war.\par \par \uc2 "We don't see our growth path in conflict with G20 pledges," Themba Maseko told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 But analysts said South Africa's plan could herald more aggressive use of both a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and low interest rates over coming years in an effort to tackle unemployment, which Zuma's government has identified as its biggest challenge. (for a graphic, click {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/kat32q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/kat32q}}}\uc2  )\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's statement suggested "another change of the monetary policy committee's (MPC) mandate is on the way, plus more \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy change", said Peter Attard Montalto, emerging markets economist at \uc2 Nomura International\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 "I think this is a push for more activist policy on both \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and MPC, involving new \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a shift of the MPC mandate to explicit growth targeting over time."\par \par \uc2 BUDGET REVIEW\par \par \uc2 Chabane did not elaborate on Tuesday on how \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  would conduct its "monetary policy \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", or say how much it wanted to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The minister of finance will make further pronouncements on the growth plan and possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans on Wednesday," Maseko said.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Pravin Gordhan, who has himself spoken out in the past against efforts by countries to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , will deliver his medium-term budget review on Wednesday. [ID:nLDE69I0YK]\par \par \uc2 The rand has appreciated about 27 percent against the U.S. dollar since the start of 2009, buoyed by a flood of investor funds from sluggish developed economies into emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts said the country would have difficulty fighting this trend. South Africa has relatively low \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and relies on foreign capital inflows to plug its current account deficit, so it cannot easily copy countries such as China and Brazil, which have used \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and taxes on capital flows to steer their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  is but a very small boat on a very rough sea in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war arena. It is beyond its capacity to steer the exchange rate of the rand directly," said Jac Laubscher, group economist at finance house Sanlam.\par \par \uc2 "Its only hope is to use its position in the G20 to promote a multilateral response to the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  realignment... Apart from that, any country that runs a perpetual current account deficit can hardly afford to discourage capital inflows."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Also, it is not clear if South Africa's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is independent of the government, would go along with any plan to weaken the rand. It might be reluctant to undertake any major campaign of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; in September it said it was accumulating foreign reserves but that the process was "costly".\par \par \uc2 Similarly, it might resist the idea of cutting interest rates to weaken the rand as its core mandate is to protect price stability. Gordhan wrote to Reserve Bank Governor Gill Marcus in February saying the MPC must also take into account economic growth and job creation in rate decisions, but it is unclear if the government would go as far as formally changing the mandate.\par \par \uc2 For those reasons, some analysts said the talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation might largely aim at satisfying the labour unions, rather than being a firm commitment to a much weaker rand.\par \par \uc2 The new plan "is much more focused on employment creation and domestic growth generation than necessarily the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", said Leon Myburgh, sub-Saharan Africa specialist at Citi.\par \par \uc2 "It's a very broad intention and the rand is just a subset of that. It's being viewed as a tool to get to an end objective, which is ultimately employment growth. I wouldn't overstate the role of the rand within the broader statement."\par \par \uc2 The rand did not move significantly against the dollar in response to Chabane's statement on Tuesday, reflecting doubts about authorities' ability to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  any time soon.\par \par \uc2 "It's more long-term, decades type of stuff -- he has made long-term comments. The budget announcements will probably have much more direct effect on markets," said Ion de Vleeschauwer, chief dealer at Bidvest Bank. (Additional reporting by Gugulakhe Lourie, Ed Cropley and Xola Potelwa; Editing by Marius Bosch and Andrew Torchia) (stella.mapenzauswa@thomsonreuters.com; +27 11 775 3161; Reuters Messaging: stella.mapenzauswa.thomsonreuters.com@reuters.net)) (For more Africa cover visit: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://af.reuters.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://af.reuters.com}}}\uc2  -- To comment on this 