\par\par \b \uc2 FOCUS: Europe's Emerging Markets Embrace  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katie Martin  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2010\par 13:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--Emerging markets could be set to indulge in a new era of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Poland last week zapped the markets with a zloty-weakening sting.\par \par \uc2 Poland's apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on April 9 to pull back the zloty--its first in 10 years--shows a strong distaste for export-hampering \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength as the global economic recovery begins to take hold, and it hints that Europe could start to mimic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -management techniques that are common in Asia.\par \par \uc2 Russia already takes frequent action to manage the level of the ruble, but the region's freely floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have generally been left to do just that: float.\par \par \uc2 Following last week's move on the zloty, however, analysts warn that further action from Poland could be on the way. It isn't alone: small-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already suspected in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whose \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 --the rand--is generally treated as though it is from one of Europe's emerging economies. The risk of a substantial hit there is growing.\par \par \uc2 "The rand is expensive. There's no question about that," said Nigel Rendell, an emerging-markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at The Royal Bank of Canada Capital Markets in London.\par \par \uc2 Rendell said he suspects that the South African authorities have been selling the rand frequently of late as it has nudged up to its strongest levels against the dollar since August 2008.\par \par \uc2 However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have so far been on a small scale. Now, particularly if the rand makes a fresh move higher, "I would not rule out a big sting," he said.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  agreed, noting that while the \uc2 South African Reserve Bank\uc2  has shied away from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent years, fresh comments from officials this month signal a shift in tactics.\par \par \uc2 Any move in the dollar below current levels of around ZAR7.30 to ZAR7.20 could easily attract new rand-buyers, pumping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swiftly higher. That, \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  said, would very probably draw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the market to limit the climb.\par \par \uc2 Feeble interest rates in major economies such as the U.S., the U.K. and the euro zone have pushed investors to search for higher returns elsewhere in the past year or so, boosting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in South Africa, for example, with its still-high rate of 6.5%. As the global economy has recovered, investors have also moved back into risky assets, bolstering the rise in these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For Poland, that pressure became too much last week, after months in which its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had become one of the most widely favored bets in the world for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors.\par \par \uc2 The euro had plunged to a 17-month low against the zloty just over PLN3.82 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acted to slow the descent. Analysts see little chance that this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or any later such moves, will do any more than slow the zloty's climb. The country's robust economy, with little if any prospect of falling interest rates, still makes the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  an attractive bet.\par \par \uc2 Still, the decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  gives a sharp signal that buying the zloty is no risk-free bet, deflecting some short-term inflows.\par \par \uc2 Attention is now turning to which other countries are in line to take action on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength. Hungary is an unlikely candidate, because it is still in interest-rate-cutting mode, which itself limits \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains. The Czech koruna, however, "is a possibility," said Rendell at RBC.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  mightn't be the right answer to boosting exports, though. In research issued last week, Stuart Bennett, a senior strategist at French bank \uc2 Credit Agricole Corporate & Investment Bank\uc2 , found that euro-zone growth rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates is the key determinant of economic strength in the region's neighboring emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The zloty, Hungarian forint and Czech koruna are all overvalued, Bennett said, and that isn't helpful to exports. But "further appreciation should not derail these economies" as long as the euro-zone recovery remains intact.\par \par \uc2 -By Katie Martin, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 (0) 207 842 9346; katie.martin@dowjones.com [ 04-15-10 0711ET ]\par \par \uc2 5008  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100415e64f0007p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
