\par\par \b \uc2 S.Africa cbank reiterates no  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  peg: report\b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2010\par 10:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg requires large reserves\par \par \uc2  * Rand hits new 20-month high against dollar\par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, April 7 - South Africa's Reserve Bank has again ruled out pegging the rand against the dollar despite worries over the strength of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Business Report newspaper said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2  Both the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have in the last few months expressed concern that the stronger rand undermines export competitiveness and therefore economic growth, but say  the need for a stable, competitive exchange rate does not translate into fixing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Business Report quoted Reserve Bank head of economic research Johan van den Heever as telling legislators that maintaining a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg required large \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2  He used the example of China, which has amassed huge volumes of foreign reserves in the process of keeping the yuan's value pegged to the dollar.\par \par \uc2  "If you have a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, then you need much (larger) foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves," van den Heever was quoted as saying. "They (China) have accumulated foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves on a scale that one cannot believe."\par \par \uc2  Allies of \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ruling ANC have pushed for the government to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the rand, saying it has hurt the manufacturing sector, now slowly recovering after its plunge last year pushed the country into recession, leading to massive job losses.\par \par \uc2  The rand <ZAR=D3> gained about 30 percent against the dollar last year and hit a new 20-month high of 7.1950 earlier on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2  Last month National Treasury Director General Lesetja Kganyago said South Africa needed to find ways of moderating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility but fixing the rand at a set level would be hard to implement and costly.[ID:nLDE62M14K]  (Reporting by Stella Mapenzauswa; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)    \par \par \uc2 SAFRICA-RAND/|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|SF|AFN|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100407e647000gh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
