\par\par \b \uc2 DJ S African  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor: Won't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  On Rand\b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2009\par 07:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to build its reserves as conditions allow, but will maintain its policy of not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets despite concerns over the strength of the rand, Deputy Governor Daniel Mminele said.\par \par \uc2 "The floating exchange-rate regime helped to cushion South Africa from more severe effects of the global crisis," Mminele said in a speech delivered in Johannesburg late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The appreciation in emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the rand, over recent months has largely been driven by external factors such as the depreciation of the dollar, increased global liquidity and renewed investor appetite for more risky assets, Mminele said.\par \par \uc2 "These gains, unfortunately, increase the likelihood of an uneven economic recovery," he said.\par \par \uc2 Tito Mboweni, who steps down this month after more than a decade as governor of the \uc2 South African Reserve Bank\uc2 , has on several occasions this year expressed concern about the effects of the strengthening rand.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened somewhat in recent weeks, but remains up about 18% since the start of the year against the dollar and 14% against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Mminele, who in June was appointed deputy governor by President Jacob Zuma from the start of July, said the Reserve Bank would continue with a strategy of accumulating \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves when market conditions are conducive.\par \par \uc2 "Over the past year, reserves accumulation was constrained by the volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the level of global risk aversion and cost considerations," he said. "More recently, conditions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have been somewhat more favorable."\par \par \uc2 -By Robb M. Stewart, Dow Jones Newswires; +27 11 783 7848; robb.stewart@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 04, 2009 01:55 ET (06:55 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020091104e5b400180\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
