\par\par \b \uc2 S.Africa cbank's Mminele sees no rand  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2009\par 07:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Cbank says too strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may cause damage\par \par \uc2 * Will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken rand\par \par \uc2 * Building reserves when can\par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, Nov 4 (Reuters) - The rand remaining too strong for too long may harm the economy but \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep to its policy of not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to manage the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Daniel Mminele said.\par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank will continue its strategy of building up reserves, though, when market conditions allow, he said.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <ZAR=D3> has lost ground over the past two weeks yet is still around 20 percent stronger against the dollar this year and has gained about 15 percent on the euro.\par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank Governor Tito Mboweni and Finance Minister Pravin Gordhan have both suggested the rand is too strong.\par \par \uc2 Mminele said appreciation in emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the rand, had mostly been driven by external factors, such as increased global liquidity, the depreciation of the dollar and renewed risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 "Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have also appreciated significantly, the rand being no exception," he said in a speech late on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remaining at non-competitive levels for too long might have adverse consequences for the real economy. Some countries opted to deal with \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  perceived to be too strong through a combination of verbal and actual market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The rand's strength has added to pressure on the manufacturing sector, which has been hard hit by a global downturn and helped pull Africa's biggest economy into its first recession in nearly two decades.\par \par \uc2 Mminele reiterated government policy that the country was committed to a floating exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 "Whilst the monetary and fiscal authorities in South Africa have at times expressed concern about the impact of the appreciated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the overall macroeconomic balance, SARB policy remains that of no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with the objective of managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 The bank would, however, continue with its strategy of accumulating reserves when market conditions allow. This had been constrained over the past year due to volatile markets and cost factors.\par \par \uc2 "More recently, conditions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have been somewhat more favourable, allowing the Bank to increase its purchases of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a responsible manner," Mminele said. (Reporting by Gordon Bell; Editing by Matthew Tostevin)\par \par \uc2 SAFRICA-MMINELE/|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SF|AFN|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091104e5b4000bw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
