\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ UPDATE: S Africa Govt, Ctrl Bk Deny Plans To Fix Rand Rate\b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2009\par 16:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, economist comment) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Robb M. Stewart and Katie Martin \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG (Dow JONES)--South Africa's recently created Economic Development Ministry Thursday said it isn't planning to freeze the exchange rate of the rand, and the governor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said its policy continues to be to maintain a floating exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The comments refute an internet report that such a plan was in the works to stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the economy.\par \par \uc2 "It is completely unfounded," Zubeida Jaffer, spokeswoman for Economic Development Minister Ebrahim Patel, told Dow Jones Newswires. "We were completely taken by surprise" by the report, she said.\par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank Governor Tito Mboweni said he wasn't aware of any plans to change South Africa's exchange rate policy, which is set by the National Treasury in consultation. Mboweni made the comment on national television after the monetary policy committee left the bank's benchmark repurchase rate at 7%.\par \par \uc2 The rand pulled back some 2% against the dollar in early trading as traders reacted nervously to the report on online news site Sake24.com, although the weakness was roughly in line with Europe's emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At 1343 GMT, the rand had recovered to 7.4717 to the dollar from a close Wednesday at 7.4100.\par \par \uc2 "They [\b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] did have a fixed exchange rate and they have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past, but it all ended in tears and I don't think they would go back down that route. It would be a huge step backwards," said Nigel Rendell, emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 Afrikaans-language Sake24, without citing sources, reported that Patel, who also is general secretary of the Southern African Clothing and Textile Workers' Union, was to propose freezing the rand at a predetermined rate.\par \par \uc2 It said the economic development minister was working with Minister of Higher Education and Training Blade Nzimande, the general secretary of the South African Communist Party, to formulate a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the country's growth rate and accelerate job creation.\par \par \uc2 President Jacob Zuma established the Ministry of Economic Development in May, a month after he was elected. The ministry's focus is on economic policymaking.\par \par \uc2 "The whole episode is symptomatic of the pressures that recession and the lack of economic progress [are] exerting on the governing coalition," \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  analysts said in a research report.\par \par \uc2 Such concerns are a good argument to attach some risk premium to the rand, the analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The coalition includes the African National Congress, the Congress of South African Trade Unions and the South African Communist Party.\par \par \uc2 -By Robb M. Stewart and Katie Martin, Dow Jones Newswires; +27 11 783 7848; robb.stewart@dowjones.com katie.martin@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 22, 2009 10:20 ET (14:20 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020091022e5am004b3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
