\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-IMF cash boosts S.Africa net reserves\b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2009\par 08:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * S.Africa reserves up sharply on IMF allocation\par \par \uc2 * Allocation part of global funding programme\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background, quotes)\par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, Sept 7 (Reuters) - South Africa received more than $2 billion in funds from the International Monetary Fund in August, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Monday, driving its net reserves up 6.49 percent to $36.922 billion.\par \par \uc2 The IMF transferred $2.166 billion to Africa's biggest economy as part of a special drawing rights equivalent of $250 billion earmarked for member countries to help deal with the global economic crisis.\par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank said in a statement on its Web site that net reserves, known as the net liquidity position, climbed from $34.67 billion in July.\par \par \uc2 Gross reserves were at $37.953 billion in August from $35.747 billion, with foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings leaping $2.158 billion to $34.156 billion.\par \par \uc2 "The change in gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves was mainly due to the general allocation of SDR 1.385 billion ($2.166 billion) from the IMF, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Bank and valuation adjustments," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The IMF money is allocated to member countries according to their quota, which is based on its relative size in the world economy. South Africa's quota is SDR 1.868 billion.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the data showed the bank did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to boost reserves itself despite the rand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remaining relatively strong against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Suffice to say that if you exclude the SDR there has been very little in terms of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Gerorge Glynos, managing director of market analysts ETM, said.\par \par \uc2 The rand <ZAR=D3> was marginally weaker at 7.64 to the dollar at 0700 GMT from before the data was released, just off a 13-month high hit late on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The IMF agreed to disburse the funds after central banks in some countries pumped money into banking systems and markets to boost liquidity at the height of the financial crisis.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support local banks, which remained relatively stable through the turmoil, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened sharply in late 2008 and equity markets fell, slowing the build up of reserves.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been steadily building up holdings over the past 5 years after it brought a long-standing negative position into balance in 2004, but gross reserves still lag those in other emerging economies. (Reporting by Gordon Bell; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 SAFRICA-RESERVES/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|AFN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SF|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090907e597000fd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
