\par\par \b \uc2 South African Markets - Factors to watch on June 10\b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2009\par 07:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, June 10 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves and political events may affect South African markets on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS\par \par \uc2 Commodity-related shares led Asian stocks higher on Wednesday, snapping a two-day decline, after metals and oil prices rallied on a decline in the U.S. dollar and as hopes grew for stronger Chinese industrial demand.\par \par \uc2 For a story, please double click on [ID:nL9288156]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH AFRICAN MARKETS\par \par \uc2 South Africa's rand firmed against the dollar on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced the appointment of a new deputy govenor and as the dollar fell against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Local stocks rebounded, with the JSE Top-40 index <.JTOPI> of blue chips gaining 0.44 percent to 20,812.10 points, while the wider All-share index <.JALSH> rose 0.44 percent at 23,049.43 points.\par \par \uc2 For Tuesday's South African financial markets closing report, double click on [ID:nL91010365]\par \par \uc2 BHP BILLITON\par \par \uc2 Miner \uc2 BHP Billiton Ltd\uc2 /Plc has accepted a 58 percent cut in metallurgical coal prices for the current shipping year with key global customers, the company said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 For story double click on [ID:nSYU006668]\par \par \uc2 MTN , VODACOM\par \par \uc2 Kuwait's Mobile Telecomunications Co (ZAIN) may sell its African business to an unnamed French company for $12 billion, Business Day newspaper said, quoting Kuwaiti paper Al Qabas, which did not provide sources.\par \par \uc2 MTN, which is in exclusive merger talks with India's Bharti \uc2 Airtel\uc2  , tried to buy the African network, previously Celtel, four years ago but was pipped by Zain. Both MTN and South Africa's Vodacom have been looking for acquisitions in Africa.\par \par \uc2 Zain shares surged on Sunday on rumours the operator may hand over management of its African \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a French telecoms firm in return for a stake in the French operator.\par \par \uc2 NASPERS\par \par \uc2 E-commerce portal Allegro, a Polish unit of South African Naspers , will buy an 18.4 percent stake in Internet portal Bankier.pl from \uc2 MCI Management\uc2  , MCI said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 For story double click on [ID:nL91047752]\par \par \uc2 RAINBOW CHICKEN\par \par \uc2 Rainbow Chicken\uc2  reports a 40 percent drop in annual headline earnings and said it only expected a substantial fall in feed prices in the second half of the new financial year.\par \par \uc2 For story double click on [ID:nWEA6214]\par \par \uc2 GOLD <XAU=>\par \par \uc2 Gold rose on Wednesday, supported by its appeal as a hedge against dollar weakness and worries about future inflation risks.\par \par \uc2 For the latest precious metals report, double click on [GOL/]\par \par \uc2 WALL STREET\par \par \uc2 The Nasdaq rose on Tuesday after an improved outlook from \uc2 Texas Instruments\uc2  lifted technology stocks, but news that 10 big banks will repay TARP funds failed to stir investor enthusiasm.\par \par \uc2 For the New York stock market report, double click on [.N]\par \par \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS\par \par \uc2 For the top emerging markets news, double click on [nTOPEMRG]\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 Some of the main stories out of the South African press:\par \par \uc2 BUSINESS DAY\par \par \uc2 - Embattled state firms could be sold off - minister\par \par \uc2 - Mboweni shrugs off union threat\par \par \uc2 - FirstRand Group appoints first black CEO\par \par \uc2 - Banks keen on deposit insurance\par \par \uc2 BUSINESS REPORT\par \par \uc2 - Mboweni will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in rand trade\par \par \uc2 - Six foreign banks plan to quit \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  - PwC\par \par \uc2 THE STAR\par \par \uc2 - Gauteng premier gest gough on graft, non-delivery\par \par \uc2 - Judiciary's independence upheld, Zuma says\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Rebecca Harrison)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SAFRICA-FACTORS/|LANGEN|SF|AFN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090610e56a000ao\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
