\par\par \b \uc2 S.Africa's rand firmer vs dlr, miners lift stocks\b0\par\par\uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2009\par 18:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rand firmer against sliding dollar\par \par \uc2 * Local stocks rebound on miners\par \par \uc2 * Govt appoints new deputy governor\par \par \uc2 * Mboweni says no change in stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Government bonds firmer\par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, June 9 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rand firmed against the dollar on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced the appointment of a new deputy governor and as the dollar fell against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The market welcomed the appointment of Daniel Mminele as the new deputy governor. Mminele, who is currently an executive general manager and has been with the Bank since 1999, was seen as experienced.\par \par \uc2 "His appointment looks positive from a market perspective given that he is a strong proponent of the current monetary policy framework, including inflation targeting," said market analysts 4CAST in a note.\par \par \uc2 Local stocks rebounded, with the JSE Top-40 index <.JTOPI> of blue chips gaining 0.44 percent to 20,812.10 points, while the wider All-share index <.JALSH> rose 0.44 percent at 23,049.43 points.\par \par \uc2 The rand <ZAR=D3> firmed 0.74 percent firmer than Monday's New York close to 8.0810 against the dollar at 1540 GMT.\par \par \uc2 "Dollar weakness is what is helping the rand," said Neil Barnard, dealer at Global Trader.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also firmed slightly after Reserve Bank Governor Tito Mboweni said the bank would not act to influence the level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said the bank had not changed its stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mboweni repeated that that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to try to build up its reserves when possible.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said strong gains in mining stocks aided by a weaker dollar lifted the bourse. "We see the market benefiting from a weaker dollar at the moment, particularly on the commodities side," Ferdi Heyneke, portfolio manager at Afrifocus Securities said.\par \par \uc2 Impala Platinum\uc2  was the biggest gainer amongst the local blue chips, advancing 3.86 percent to 187.10 rand and diversified miner African Rainbow Minerals climbed 2.61 percent to 143.65 rand.\par \par \uc2 Gold stocks were among the top performers, led by the world's fourth-biggest gold producer Gold Fields which increased 3.52 percent to 99.12 rand and \uc2 AngloGold Ashanti\uc2  was up 1.60 percent to 319.53 rand as bullion price firmed while the dollar weakened against the euro.\par \par \uc2 But shares in FirstRand -- which has appointed Sizwe Nxasana, the head of its core banking unit as its new chief executive -- regained lost ground to close 0.98 percent higher to 13.44 rand.\par \par \uc2 However, Telkom shares recover lost ground to close at 0.90 percent higher to 35.90 rand, despite being rated with Vodacom as "neutral" in a research note by Nomura brokerage. Vodacom fell 1.55 percent to 54.64 rand.\par \par \uc2 South Africa's government bonds were firmer, in line with the rand. The yield on the 2015 issue <ZAR157=> was down 1 basis point to 8.425 percent and that on the 2036 note <ZAR209=> fell 3.5 basis points to 8.535 percent. (Reporting by Phumza Macanda and Pakama Ngceni; Editing by Andy Bruce)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SAFRICA/CLOSE|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SF|AFN|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090609e5690017z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
