\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Markets-Stks plunge 7 pct, Russia suspends trade\b0\par\par\uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2008\par 12:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Emerging stks lowest in 3 years\par \par \uc2 * Sovereign debt spreads widest in 4 years\par \par \uc2 * Russian bourses plunge before trade suspension\par \par \uc2 * Ukrainian hryvnia falls to record low, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen\par \par \uc2 * Icelandic crown plunges 23 pct vs euro\par \par \uc2 By Sebastian Tong\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Emerging assets were hammered on Wednesday as government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the world to shore up the banking sector failed to stem panic-selling by investors unnerved by the worst financial crisis in some 80 years.\par \par \uc2 Fears of a global recession roiled global markets, sending the emerging equities index <.MSCIEF> over 7 percent down to its lowest level in three years and benchmark emerging sovereign debt spreads <11EMJ> to their widest in four years.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's PFTS stock exchange <.PFTSI><0#.PFTSI> remained suspended for a second day while Russia, one of the four biggest component economies in the MSCI Emerging Markets Index, suspended share trading after steep falls in the first minutes of the session.\par \par \uc2 "Markets are down pretty much across the board. It started with equities on Wall Street and the rout continued in Asia, with central banks trying to prop up equity markets and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Nigel Rendell, senior emerging markets strategist at RBC.\par \par \uc2 "The implications for the real economy are quite severe."\par \par \uc2 By 1020 GMT, the emerging stocks index had fallen 7.27 percent to 611.19 while the emerging sovereign debt benchmark was 9 basis points wider to trade at 512 bps over U.S. Treasuries <11EMJ>.\par \par \uc2 Russia's rouble-denominated MICEX <.MCX> index fell over 14 percent in the first 35 minutes of trade before regulators imposed a two-day suspension. Its RTS index <.IRTS> slid over 11.25 percent before the exchange moved to suspend trade. [ID:nL8646384]\par \par \uc2 FUNDING PROBLEMS\par \par \uc2 Emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended recent losses as investors continued to unwind high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to head for the relative safety of the Japanese yen.\par \par \uc2 "Funding for emerging market governments and corporates remains a crucial issue. As there are less U.S. dollar funds available, reflected in the surge of money market rates and spreads, local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have come under pressure," \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Iceland's crown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank around 23 percent to 195.41 against the euro <EURISK=>, a day after the country set its exchange rate at 131 against the euro against the backdrop of the country's deepening banking crisis.\par \par \uc2 Iceland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied fixing the exchange rate and said the exchange rate level of 131 crowns per euro reflected its view that recent \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels were unrealistic. [ID:nSAT005674]\par \par \uc2 The island nation is seeking a 4 billion euro ($5 billion) loan from Russia to bolster its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to help prop a banking sector that is tottering under $73 billion in external debt.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's hryvnia <UAH=> skidded to an all-time low of 5.9 against the dollar, prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID;nL837657]\par \par \uc2 Investors also sold \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rand <ZAR=> \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which fell 4 percent to six-year lows against the dollar, further pressured by news that senior members of its ruling African National Congress party could break away from the movement. [ID:nJAT003842]\par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira <TRY=>, another bellwether emerging market, fell 2.4 percent versus the dollar while Turkey's benchmark dollar bond <TRGLB30=RR> saw its yield rise nearly 25 basis points. (Additional reporting by Carolyn Cohn; Editing by Victoria Main)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081011e4a800091\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
