\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-S.Africa cbank-inflation expectations deteriorating\b0\par\par\uc2 By Stella Mapenzauswa   \par \uc2 817 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 2008\par 17:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds more Mboweni comments)\par \par \uc2 PRETORIA, May 13 (Reuters) - South Africa's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday inflation was expected to rise, but that it remained committed to bringing the gauge within target range "over a reasonable time horizon".\par \par \uc2 The targeted CPIX consumer inflation gauge has persisted above the top end of a 3-6 percent range since April 2007, and accelerated to a new five-year high of 10.1 percent year-on-year in March.\par \par \uc2 "The inflation outlook has deteriorated since the publication of the previous monetary policy review in November 2007," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a twice-yearly monetary policy review.\par \par \uc2 "The bank's current expectation is for inflation to peak in the near term and then follow a downward trend to return to within the target range by the end of 2009."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy committee has lifted the key repo rate by a cumulative 450 basis points to 11.5 percent since June 2006, partly to curb inflationary credit-driven consumer demand.\par \par \uc2 "The MPC remains committed to bringing inflation back to within the target range over a reasonable time horizon," the bank said in its review on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 It said by the final quarter of 2007 there were clear signs that tighter monetary policy was beginning to impact on demand, but that the economy was faced with a number of exogenous supply-side shocks that were impacting on the inflation outlook.\par \par \uc2 "Initially, these shocks were confined to oil and food prices, but more recently electricity price developments also compounded the problems," it said.\par \par \uc2 "The possibility of further electricity price increases appears the most significant and immediate upside risk."\par \par \uc2 State power utility Eskom [ESCJ.UL], struggling to meet rising demand for electricity, has applied to the national energy regulator for a 53 percent tariff increase to help finance its recapitalisation programme. The regulator will rule on the application in June.\par \par \uc2 POSITIVE REGIONAL OUTLOOK\par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank said a 14.2 percent increase in the electricity tariff already approved in April, the possibility of another rise and a weaker rand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had worsened the inflation outlook.\par \par \uc2 The bank said the rand had depreciated by approximately six percent against the U.S. dollar since November 2007 and around 25 percent against the euro, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of South Africa's major trading partner, the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 Electricity supply constraints may also have affected investor perceptions towards South Africa and "there appears to be an increased risk premium that investors require for holding the rand", the Reserve Bank said.\par \par \uc2 In a briefing to business leaders on the review, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Tito Mbowni dismissed suggestions \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  take steps to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the rand stable.\par \par \uc2 "We are not going to do anything of the sort ... The \uc2 South African Reserve Bank\uc2  is not in the business of managing the exchange rate, we are in the business of targeting inflation".\par \par \uc2 He said South Africa's inflation rate should be in line with those of its major trading partners, and monetary policy has to tighen due to generalised inflation pressures.\par \par \uc2 "We can't just say that the inflation problem that we are facing is only because of food and energy, it's more generalised, and therefore monetary policy has to respond to that. It's very clear that monetary policy has to tighten a bit."\par \par \uc2 In its review, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the regional economic outlook remained positive, but tensions over neighbouring Zimbabwe's disputed presidential election posed a downside risk.\par \par \uc2 Electoral officials in Zimbabwe say the main opposition candidate defeated veteran President Robert Mugabe in the March 29 election, but failed to garner enough ballots to avoid a second round vote. The opposition MDC insists that it won outright, and that Mugabe manipulated the result.\par \par \uc2 "Africa's economic outlook remains positive given the continued favourable commodity price outlook, regional macroeconomic stability, rising oil production and continued capital inflows," the Reserve Bank said.\par \par \uc2 "The most important downside risks for growth in the region would comprise heightened risk aversion by investors as a result of the tensions flowing from the Zimbabwe elections."\par \par \uc2 South Africa holds its own elections next year, but Mboweni said the new incoming government was not likely to interfere with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's independence.\par \par \uc2 "I think there's a depth of leadership in South Africa which would not seek to undermine that which is in the constitution of the Republic, which says very clearly that the \uc2 South African Reserve Bank\uc2  ... shall pursue it's objectives freely, independently, without fear or favour."\par \par \uc2 (For full Reuters Africa coverage and to have your say on the top issues, visit: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://africa.reuters.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://africa.reuters.com/}}}\uc2 ) (Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 SAFRICA-INFLATION/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|SF|AFN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080513e45d001oq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
