\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-SAfrica economic advisers call for rand  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gordon Bell   \par \uc2 705 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2008\par 15:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds Treasury comment paras 6-10, background)\par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, May 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable and "competitive", and should maintain its inflation targets, a group advising the government said.\par \par \uc2 In its report released on Thursday, an international panel -- known as the Harvard Group -- also suggested a budget surplus of between 1 and 2 percent to help ease inflation and for exchange controls to be scrapped.\par \par \uc2 The international panel, known as the Harvard Group, were asked to assess South Africa's economic policies and propose ways to boost growth and cut unemployment.\par \par \uc2 "Maintain the current inflation targeting regime but adopt a strategy that pays more attention to the level and stability of the real exchange rate," it said.\par \par \uc2 "This involves the use of SARB (\uc2 South African Reserve Bank\uc2 ) statements on the exchange rate when it deviates from what the bank considers compatible with external and internal balance. In addition, it (SARB) should be willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to back up its statement."\par \par \uc2 National Treasury Director-General Lesetja Kganyago said that government had long identified \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility as a constraint and had increased \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in the past three years.\par \par \uc2 "What is new about the international panel recommendations is that it said we needed to continue to accumulate reserves more aggressively than we had done in the past."\par \par \uc2 "I would say the amount of reserves we have amassed over the past three years is quite significant, but for now... we will consider the recommendations and decide if we take them forward," he said.\par \par \uc2 South Africa brought a long-standing negative reserves position into balance early in 2004 with the elimination of its loss-making forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  book -- historically seen as a weak point for the rand.\par \par \uc2 Net gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $33.125 billion at the end of March.\par \par \uc2 The rand was 10 percent weaker to the dollar so far this year, but had held firm for several years after plunging to an all-time low of 13.85 in December 2001.\par \par \uc2 Kganyago said government had no control over daily \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements. T\par \par \uc2 "What we do have control of is macro economic policy, and we believe our macro economic policy is prudent and correct."\par \par \uc2 The Treasury stressed that the report, submitted in 2007, did not reflect government views and that it had neither adopted nor rejected any of the recommendations.\par \par \uc2 Kganyago would not comment about calls from leftist quarters in the ruling ANC to relax inflation targeting.\par \par \uc2 "I cannot comment on the ruling party, but the resolutions of the ruling party are very clear: that we need to continue with the prudent macro economic policy stance for growth and poverty reduction."\par \par \uc2 Disillusioned by widespread poverty almost 14 years after the end of apartheid, communists and labour movement allies of the ANC helped Jacob Zuma win the party presidency in December, hoping he would push for more pro-poor policies.\par \par \uc2 However, Finance Minister Trevor Manuels and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Tito Mboweni have in the past said inflation targeting was here to stay.\par \par \uc2 STICK TO GROWTH TARGET\par \par \uc2 Kganyago said the Treasury was sticking to its current economic growth forecast of 4 percent for 2008, despite signs that higher interest rates were weighing on local demand.\par \par \uc2 The SARB has raised the repo rate by 450 basis points to 11.5 percent since June 2006, to arrest CPIX inflation that has stayed above its 3 - 6 percent since April 2007.\par \par \uc2 "When we made our forecasts we took cognisance of what will be the trajectory of monetary policy and global economy ... We are sticking with (it) and will only revise it in (October)."\par \par \uc2 Consumer confidence was at a four-year low while business confidence fell to a four-and-half year low.\par \par \uc2 The manufacturing industry -- the second biggest in the economy -- shrunk by 1.1 percent in March, and analysts said it was a bad omen for economic growth this year. (Additional Reporting by Phumza Macanda, Editing by Ron Askew\par \par \uc2 SAFRICA-ECONOMY/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|AFN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080508e458001ir\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw90\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1350\pichgoal600
