eated by \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 AngloGold\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ashanti's greenfields exploration teams, at three key prospects,      \par namely Tropicana (Western Australia), Mongbwalu (DRC) and Gramalote (Colombia). \par Other additions include 17.1Moz at Mponeng, and 4.7 Moz at CC&V, both due to    \par improved economics and revised methodologies.                                   \par BROWNFIELDS EXPLORATION                                                         \par In South Africa , surface drilling continued in the Project Zaaiplaats area,    \par with borehole MZA9, a long deflection to the east in progress, and drilling at  \par borehole MMB5 continued.                                                        \par Surface drilling in the Moab North area has been re-started after the           \par structural interpretation was updated. Borehole MCY4 has been re-opened and a   \par deflection to the east is in progress and borehole MCY5 advanced 1,606m during  \par the quarter.                                                                    \par At Tau Lekoa, borehole G54 was started during the quarter and intersected       \par poorly developed Venterdorp Contact Reef at 1,097m and deflection drilling      \par continues.                                                                      \par At Iduapriem in Ghana , resource conversion (RC) drilling at Blocks 7 and 8 was \par completed in November 2007. An additional 19 holes were drilled during the      \par quarter, in an effort to convert inferred mineral resources to indicated miner  \par al resources . Modelling has commenced.                                         \par In Australia, at Boddington mine, three rigs were employed on resource          \par conversion and near mine extension exploration diamond drilling. During the     \par quarter, approximately 16,263m of drilling from 17 holes was completed, and     \par for the year, a total of 121,212m from 151 holes was drilled.                   \par In Brazil, at Corrego do Sitio Sulphide Project, drilling continued at          \par Laranjeira and Carvoaria ore bodies (Paraiso). At the Lamego project, surface   \par and underground exploration of the Carruagem and Arco da Velha zones is         \par progressing. At Cuiaba Mine, the narrow- vein subsidiary orebodies, notably     \par Balancao, were explored with the objective to obtain additional ore and         \par enhance mining flexibility.                                                     \par At Siguiri in Guinea, exploration activities focused on 25m by 25m of infill    \par RC drilling at Kintinian (situated 4km north of the plant), and 50m by 50m of   \par infill RC drilling at Sintroko South (situated 8km south of the mine).          \par Reconnaissance aircore drilling commenced on the coincident AEM and geochemical \par anomalies at Kouremale in Block 4, close to the Malian border, and in Block 3   \par at Kolita and Kounkoun. These targets are located approximately 70km and 35km,  \par respectively north east of the current infrastructure.                          \par At Geita in Tanzania, exploration activities continued to be concentrated in    \par five areas , namely, Matandani Pit; Area 3; Nyakabale-Prospect 30; the Lone     \par Cone -Nyankanga Gap and the Nyankanga foot wall. Infill drilling was also       \par started at the Star and Comet projects.                                         \par At Morila in Mali , a programme of four diamond drill holes was completed       \par during the quarter. These boreholes were targeted at extensions of the          \par mineralisation in prospective areas.                                            \par Pitting was initiated at Sokela, to the South West of the mine and two trenches \par were dug in the Domba area to the North of the mine, in order to extract        \par samples for further evaluation.                                                 \par At Sadiola, a fence line of three diamond holes were drilled inside the FE4     \par main pit. The objectives of this programme was to establish the potential of    \par sulphide mineralisation in the hard rock. The fence line of 22 diamond holes b  \par etween FE3-pit 3 and FE4 was completed and borehole SDFE3S - 022 was concluded, \par as well as additional resource delineation drilling at Tambali South.           \par At Yatela, the final assay results for the "Deep Sulphide" drilling were        \par received and the results proved to be disappointing. Infill drilling at the     \par North West Extension to the Yatela deposit was started with 2,985m being        \par drilled from 66 boreholes.                                                      \par At Navachab in Namibia, drilling continued in the Upper Schist to the north-    \par west of the main pit, and drilling on the west ramp of the main pit area was    \par completed, with further drilling planned for 2008. The drilling programme to    \par test vertical mineralisation along the Upper Schist-MDM contact in the main pit \par area continued, while positive results were received from the drilling at Gecko \par South and North. Drill access roads for additional drilling in the Gecko Far    \par North and for Anomaly 16 are currently being developed.                         \par At Cripple Creek & Victor in the United States, exploration and development     \par drilling continued on the north side of the district near Schist Island and     \par Control Point.                                                                  \par GREENFIELDS EXPLORATION                                                         \par Greenfields exploration activities continued in seven countries (Australia,     \par Colombia, the DRC, China, Laos, the Philippines, and Russia) during the fourth  \par quarter of 2007. A total of 378,014m of diamond drilling (DDH), reverse         \par circulation (RC), and aircore (AC) drilling was completed during the year, and  \par drill testing at existing priority targets and delineating new targets in       \par Australia, the DRC, Colombia, and China was undertaken.                         \par A total of 6.95Moz attributable (9. 1 Moz on a 100% basis) of JORC -standard    \par Inferred and Indicated Resources were delineated by  \f28 \uc2 \f2 AngloGold\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ashanti's         \par greenfields exploration teams for the year ended December 2007 at three key     \par prospects globally, namely Tropicana (Western Australia), Mongbwalu (DRC) and   \par Gramalote (Colombia). This figure exceeds the market guidance of 6Moz given for \par the discovery of new gold resources by greenfields exploration by the end of    \par 2007. In addition, a significant drill programme and conceptual study is        \par concurrently being undertaken at  \f28 \uc2 \f2 AngloGold\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ashanti's 100% owned La Colosa       \par project in Colombia, with an additional Inferred Resources expected to be       \par announced for La Colosa during the first quarter of 2008.                       \par In Australia, drilling continued at the Tropicana JV Project ( \f28 \uc2 \f2 AngloGold\f28 \uc2 \f2          \par Ashanti 70%, Independence Group 30%) during the fourth quarter and the          \par Pre-Feasibility Study (PFS) Resource Model was completed. An initial open       \par pit resource (Inferred and Indicated) of 62.8Mt @ 2.01g/t (using a 0.6g/t       \par cut-off) for 4.05Moz (100%basis) was announced on 3 December 2007. This         \par resource was calculated using the assay data from nearly 141,000m of diamond    \par and RC drilling, at drill hole spacings of a minimum of 50m by 50m. The         \par Tropicana PFS will focus on the economics of the open -pit mining of gold       \par mineralisation currently identified over a four kilometre strike length         \par at Tropicana -Havana, and will include additional mining, metallurgical,        \par and environmental studies. Reconnaissance exploration is continuing, in         \par parallel, throughout the remainder of the Tropicana JV tenement holding,        \par particularly in the Beachcomber sector.                                         \par Regional exploration and target generation activities continued in Colombia     \par during the fourth quarter, with DDH undertaken on five prospects. A conceptual  \par economic study was also completed on the bulk-tonnage Gramalote prospect        \par (Antioquia Department), where an Inferred Resource (100% basis) of 57. 8Mt @    \par 1.14g/t (using a 0.5g/t cut-off), for a total of 2.12Moz has been delineated.   \par The Inferred Resource for Gramalote was calculated using the assay data derived \par from the 13,060m of diamond drilling (in 43 drill holes), including adit        \par sampling completed to date. Ownership of the Gramalote project is currently 75% \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 AngloGold\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ashanti, 25%  \f28 \uc2 \f2 B2Gold Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2 , however, a  non-binding memorandum   \par of understanding has been signed with B2Gold in which B2Gold will have the      \par option to earn-in to a 51% interest in the Gramalote project in return for      \par taking the project through to Feasibility.                                      \par Resource delineation drilling continued during the fourth quarter at  \f28 \uc2 \f2 AngloGold\f28 \uc2 \f2   \par Ashanti's 100% owned La Colosa porphyry gold prospect (Tolima Department). To   \par date, approximately 12,000m of diamond drilling (from 42 drill holes) has been  \par completed at La Colosa. Additional drilling and conceptual studies are both     \par being undertaken at La Colosa, with an Inferred Resource expected to be         \par announced by end of February 2008.  \f28 \uc2 \f2 AngloGold\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ashanti and JV partners have also  \par completed first-pass diamond drilling on three other projects during the        \par quarter, with follow-up drilling expected to be undertaken on one of these      \par prospects during the first quarter of 2008.                                     \par Exploration activities undertaken in Concession 40 (DRC) included the infill    \par drilling of the main mineralised mylonite zones at Mongbwalu, together with the \par initial evaluation of priority targets regionally. A conceptual economic study  \par for the Mongbwalu deposit was also completed during the quarter, and confirmed  \par an initial open pittable Inferred Resource of 33Mt @ 2.68g/t (using a 0.5g/t    \par cut -off) for 2.93Moz (2.52Moz attributable to  \f28 \uc2 \f2 AngloGold\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ashanti) at Mongbwalu. \par The initial resource area lies within a polygon that covers both the Adidi      \par sector and the Socumoto sector (which is located about 1km to the south-east of \par the past- producing Adidi mine). The conceptual study utilised the assay data   \par from the 88,000m of DDH and RC drilling that has been completed at Mongbwalu by \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 AngloGold\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ashanti between mid-2005 and November 2007.                           \par In Russia, all efforts were focused on finalising the formation of the          \par Polymetal/ \f28 \uc2 \f2 AngloGold\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ashanti Strategic Alliance. The registration of Zoloto      \par Taigi, the Russian management company, is expected to be completed during the   \par first quarter of 2008. Management of exploration activities in the four initial \par project areas (Bogunay, Anenskoye, and Veduga in the Krasnoyarsk region, and    \par Aprelskovskoye in the Chita region) was gradually assumed by the Joint Venture  \par team in late 2007. The JV was also successful in acquiring the 390km 2          \par Sovremenie Prospect (Krasno yarsk Region) at auction.                           \par In China , a short (1,053m) DDH programme was completed on the Yili-Yunlong CJV \par prospect in Xinjiang Province (northwestern China). The primary objective of    \par the drill programme was to test the vertical continuity of outcropping          \par gold-copper mineralisation, however, drilling only succeeded in intersecting    \par weakly anomalous mineralisation at depth. At Red Valley (Qinghai), assay        \par results from the 3,300m DDH programme were also reviewed and confirmed the      \par presence of only low-grade gold mineralisation within the principal targets. As \par a result,  \f28 \uc2 \f2 AngloGold\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ashanti elected to withdraw from earning into the CJV.      \par Registration of the Pingwu CJV (Sichuan province) is proceeding according to    \par schedule, with systematic exploration expected to commence on the property in   \par the first quarter of 2008.                                                      \par In the Philippines, the final tenement grant for Mapawa is still awaited from   \par the Manila Central Mines and Geosciences Bureau. Work continued on finalizing   \par the Mapawa and Outer Siana JV Agreements with Red 5 Limited.                    \par In Laos, the Strategic Exploration Alliance between  \f28 \uc2 \f2 AngloGold\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ashanti and       \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Oxiana Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  expired on 13 December 2007 and has not been extended by mutual      \par agreement.                                                                      \par Mineral Resource and Ore Reserve                                                \par Mineral Resources and Ore Reserves are reported in accordance with the minimum  \par standard described by the Australasian Code for Reporting of Exploration        \par Results, Mineral Resources and Ore Reserves (The JORC Code, 2004 Edition), and  \par also conform to the standards set out in the South African Code for the         \par Reporting of Mineral Resources and Mineral Reserves (the SAMREC 2000 Code).     \par Mineral Resources are inclusive of the Ore Reserve component unless otherwise   \par stated.                                                          