\par\par \b \uc2 South African Markets - Factors to watch on Oct 8   \b0\par\par\uc2 433 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2007\par 08:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, Oct 8 (Reuters) - The following company announcements, scheduled economic indicators, debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves and political events may affect South African markets on Monday.   \par \par \uc2  - - - - -   \par \par \uc2  Some of the main stories out of the South African press:   \par \par \uc2  BUSINESS DAY   \par \par \uc2  - Gauteng ANC vote gives Sexwale early poll lift   \par \par \uc2  - Reserve Bank faces tough call on rates   \par \par \uc2  BUSINESS REPORT   \par \par \uc2  - Mining safety audit short on skills   \par \par \uc2  - Court ruling shifts balance in cases of unfair dismissal   \par \par \uc2  THE STAR   \par \par \uc2  - Hair-raising win for Boks   \par \par \uc2  - Pikoli saga sets stage for security shake-up   \par \par \uc2  - - - -   \par \par \uc2  GLOBAL MARKETS   \par \par \uc2  Asian stocks outside of Japan hit a lifetime high on Monday, but the dollar headed lower after a solid U.S. jobs report failed to dent expectations for another cut in U.S. interest rates.   \par \par \uc2  HARMONY    \par \par \uc2  Police have recovered the dead bodies of 23 illegal miners at a South African mine of Harmony Gold Limited, the company said on Sunday.   \par \par \uc2  The 23 were caught in a fire that broke out on Sept. 18 at a disused section of Harmony's St. Helena mine in the Free State province, the company said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2  For story double click on [ID:nL07623093]   \par \par \uc2  SOUTH AFRICAN MARKETS   \par \par \uc2  South African banks guided the bourse to a high note for the fifth straight day on Friday as financials found fresh impetus from its upward global peers and positive U.S. jobs data.  For Friday's South African financial markets closing report, double click on [ID:nL0538952]   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  The dust may have settled on the global credit crisis following \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but serious risks remain, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  Reserve Bank Governor Tito Mboweni said on Friday.   \par \par \uc2  For story double click on [ID:nN05611071]   \par \par \uc2  GOLD <XAU=>   \par \par \uc2  Gold was flat on Monday, with trade thin due to holidays in Japan and the United States, and on caution ahead of U.S. Federal Reserve minutes that could give clues on interest rates.   \par \par \uc2  Gold <XAU=> was at $741.00/741.75 by 0326 GMT, down a touch from $741.10/741.90 in New York on Friday.   \par \par \uc2  For the latest precious metals report, double click on [GOL/]   \par \par \uc2  WALL STREET   \par \par \uc2  The Dow and the S&P 500 surged to all-time highs on Friday after a solid employment report rekindled optimism about the U.S. economy and corporate profits.   \par \par \uc2  For the New York stock market report, double click on [.N]   \par \par \uc2  EMERGING MARKETS   \par \par \uc2  For the top emerging markets news, double click on [nTOPEMRG]     \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SAFRICA-FACTORS/|LANGEN|SF|AFN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|RNP|DNP|PTD|PCM|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071008e3a8000fu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
