\par\par \b \uc2 PRESS DIGEST - South Africa - March 22  \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 06:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, March 22 (Reuters) - These are the leading stories in the South African press on Thursday. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy.  \par \par \uc2  - - - -  \par \par \uc2  BUSINESS DAY  \par \par \uc2  - Zambia has become the first African country to openly call for a new approach to be taken on Zimbabwe, with President Levy Mwanawasa and former president Kenneth Kaunda seperately urging African leaders to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the embattled country.  \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current account deficit widened sharply in the fourth quarter of last year and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to monitor the shortfall and possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation, says Reserve Bank Governor Tito Mboweni.  \par \par \uc2  - - - -  \par \par \uc2  BUSINESS REPORT  \par \par \uc2  - Talks between JSE-listed Phumelela  and Gold Circle, aimed at creating a single horse racing company, could be concluded soon.  \par \par \uc2  - The economic advantages of hosting major sporting events do not automatically outweigh the costs, according to Reserve Bank Governor Tito Mboweni.  \par \par \uc2  - A panel of Islamic jurists will investigate the implications for Muslim consumers of a decision by SAB   to use carbon dioxide derived from beer production in soft drinks bottled by subsidiary ABI.  \par \par \uc2  - - - -  \par \par \uc2  THE STAR  \par \par \uc2  - Bob Woolmer's family are dismayed at the rumours surrounding the death of the former South Africa cricket coach.  \par \par \uc2  - Independent Democrats leader Patricia de Lille has laid criminal charges against 29 South Africans whom she says benefitted from massively discounted luxury vehicles as a bribe in a controversial arms deal.  \par \par \uc2  - - - -  \par \par \uc2  THE CITIZEN  \par \par \uc2  - The state will try to clear another hurdle on Thursday in the process of again charging ANC Deputy President Jacob Zuma and French arms manufacturer Thint with corruption.  \par \par \uc2  - - - -  \par \par \uc2  SOWETAN  \par \par \uc2  - The Inkatha Freedom Party on Wednesday called on the government to pass a law that would force judges to hand down a sentence within two months of finding an accused guilty.  \par \par \uc2  - Access to basic services, crime education and HIV-AIDS prevention came under the spotlight on Wednesday at a Human Rights Day commemoration in Sharpville.     \par \par \uc2 SAFRICA-PRESS|LANGEN|SF|AFN|G|RBN|REVU|RNP|DNP|PGE|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070322e33m000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
