\par\par \b \uc2 S.Africa Treasury,cbank often discuss rand - govt.  \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2005\par 14:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  CAPE TOWN, May 4 (Reuters) - South Africa's Treasury and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hold regular discussions on the strength of the rand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a minister said on Wednesday, amid mounting concern over the impact of the unit's strength on jobs. The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly cut its key repo rate by half a percentage point to 7 percent last month, citing the need for a competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and worries about the impact which the rand's strength was having on parts of the economy.   \par \par \uc2  A sustained rally in the rand between 2001 and 2004 has seen it appreciate by more than 130 percent versus the dollar, eroding exports and corporate profits and sparking calls for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and help limit job losses.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's jobless rate stands at 26 percent.   \par \par \uc2  "As you are familiar with the strong rand it is continually under discussion ... between the treasury and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Public Enterprises Minister Alec Erwin told reporters. Erwin reiterated the government's wish for a "stable and competitive" exchange rate but said an inflation targeting policy introduced five years ago would remain in place.   \par \par \uc2  "The process is there to keep monitoring two aspects ... how is the Reserve Bank protecting the value of money and if certain actions are taken what will be the implications for this," he said.   \par \par \uc2  "We don't intend changing the basic policy which is inflation targeting," Erwin added.   \par \par \uc2  The annual increase in the benchmark CPIX inflation index has been inside its 3-6 percent target range for 19 consecutive months. Some local analysts believe the policy is inappropriate for an emerging economy like South Africa, which has a growth rate that lags many comparable markets.   \par \par \uc2  The rand initially weakened after the rate cut, but has since rebounded sharply, to trade at about 6.03 to the dollar from about 6.20 when the step was announced.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050504e1540038u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
