\par\par \b \uc2 S.Africa rand hits 10-wk peak,more gains possible.  \b0\par\par\uc2 699 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2004\par 16:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 JOHANNESBURG, June 21 (Reuters) - South Africa's rand jumped to a ten-week peak on Monday, bolstered by offshore demand and broad dollar weakness, with traders predicting further gains as jittery domestic exporters pile into the market.  \par \par \uc2 The volatile unit raced to 6.2850/dollar, a gain of nearly one percent during the session and its best level since April 12, according to Reuters data.  \par \par \uc2 "There has been a bit of a sentiment shift over the last 48 trading hours and looking at the market it seems chances do favour a further rand rally," said Sanlam technical analyst Jacques Potgieter.  \par \par \uc2 "If we close below 6.30/dollar - and it seems that could happen - we could go back to the 6.20/dollar level. But I'm sure the SARB (South African Reserve Bank) will step in at that point."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said it will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to affect the value of the rand, but traders say it does quicken the pace of dollar-buying to build its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves when the domestic unit firms sharply. The rand has now appreciated by about six percent against the greenback this year, building on gains of 28 percent in 2003 - a trend viewed with concern by domestic exporters, who maintain its strength is eroding their profits.  \par \par \uc2 News last Friday that the U.S. current account deficit widened to a record $144.9 billion in the first quarter of 2004, exceeding forecasts, knocked the dollar weaker against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 It propelled the euro - the unit of South Africa's main trade partner which often sets direction for the rand - to $1.2146 on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 This helped the rand rally through the key 6.45/dollar level, firming by nearly three percent to 6.35/dollar in late offshore trade.  \par \par \uc2 Its gains on Monday flew in the face of the euro's retreat to $1.2094. It broke through 6.35/dollar, another key level, on the back of dollar selling by offshore funds in London.  \par \par \uc2 "Their models say the rand could go all the way back to 6.09/dollar," a local dealer said, referring to the rand's level in December last year, which was a 46-month peak at that time.  \par \par \uc2 "But I don't think it will go below 6/dollar," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Potgieter said the rand may get a further boost from domestic inflation figures due later this week if they were substantially higher than expected - but this is seen as unlikely.  \par \par \uc2 Domestic markets are betting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key repo rate - slashed by 5.5 percentage points to eight percent last year - will rise by one percentage point later in 2004, to keep inflation pressures at bay.  \par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll predicted that consumer price data for May due on Wednesday will show that the targeted CPIX index rose by an annual rate of 4.7 percent, up from 4.4 percent in April and back within the upper end of its three to six percent target.  \par \par \uc2 Producer price data for the same month follow on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The appeal of South Africa's high interest rates - along with surging commodity prices and good economic fundamentals - has helped buoy the rand in the past year.  \par \par \uc2 South African government bonds rallied on the stronger rand, although traders said they may retreat after the inflation data.  \par \par \uc2 The yield on the benchmark R153 , due 2010, was down 11 basis points at 10.01 percent after dipping briefly to 9.99 percent. Yields on the R194 bond, due 2008, fell 12 basis points to 9.93 percent.  \par \par \uc2 - ~- - - SOUTH AFRICAN PRICES   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    All S.African gilts              Benchmark R150\par    Rand Eurobonds                   Rand cross rates\par    Rand forwards                    Rand/dollar futures\par  - - - -\par  NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS\par    All S.African news               S.African diary\par    All debt news                    S.African summary\par    S.African indicators             Index of summaries\par    Long-term forecasts              All African news\par  - - - -\par  EMERGING MARKET DEBT\par    Benchmark Brazil bond\par    Benchmark Argentine bond\par    Benchmark Mexican bond\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - ~- --  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For a complete list of Brady Bond prices on Reuters type 'BRADY' and hit the F3 key. Also see the emerging market speed guide by double-clicking on .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040621e06l001oe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
