\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-S.Africa cbank ends  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  hangover from apartheid.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Lucia Mutikani  \par \uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 14:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 PRETORIA, March 1 (Reuters) - South Africa's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended a financial hangover from the apartheid era in February when it closed its loss-making forward \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  book, enabling it to focus on building its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, it said on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The forward book - which referred to the bank's dollar purchases on the forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market - peaked at an exposure of over $25 billion in 1998, when authorities used it in a vain attempt to defend the rand from speculators.  \par \par \uc2 It was created in the 1970s during apartheid era to combat economic sanctions and it has made losses running to billions of dollars.  \par \par \uc2 "Squaring off the forward book indeed represents a significant milestone and has allowed us to finally successfully deal with one of the sad consequences of an unfortunate part of this country's history," Governor Tito Mboweni told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 It has been squared off through dollar purchases from the market, which has also seen the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gross gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rise to $8.332 billion at the end of February from $8.066 billion in January.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar purchases, which have been made possible by the strong rand, are not intended to influence the level of the exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 "Hopefully the market will read that and say hey, these folks are okay. They are doing well. Not only do those South Africans win Oscars, but they are able as well to tidy up their books in a responsible manner," said Mboweni.  \par \par \uc2 He was referring to South African actress Charlize Theron, who on Sunday won the Oscar for best actress.  \par \par \uc2 The rand was little moved at 6.62/dollar on the widely expected announcement. "It (the closing of the forward book) opens the way for gross reserves to increase in the months ahead which should be positive for South Africa's rating with the major credit agencies," said JP Morgan economist Marisa Fassler.  \par \par \uc2 APARTHEID OVERHANG  \par \par \uc2 The forward book was originally created to allow state utilities hedge their debt on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when apartheid-era sanctions made it difficult to do so, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  taking on the risk on behalf of the government.  \par \par \uc2 But when sanctions tightened during the 1980s, officials at the Reserve Bank decided to use the book to defend the rand.  \par \par \uc2 After the fall of apartheid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose dramatically during the 1998 global emerging market crisis, building up a huge loss-making position for the coming years as the rand continued to weaken. The forward book has been an obstacle preventing the Reserve Bank from building up its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves which are considered meagre by emerging market standards.  \par \par \uc2 The large forward book, which Mboweni said was "a structural overhang from apartheid," and a then negative net open foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  position (NOFP), had resulted in the rand being perceived as a one-way downward bet.  \par \par \uc2 The NOFP, often described as South Africa's "overdraft in dollars" is the difference between the bank's net reserves and forward book. The negative NOFP was eliminated in May 2003.  \par \par \uc2 "With the government unable to borrow foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (during apartheid), the country could only use one mechanism to raise foreign capital: providing forward cover to the private sector to ensure their use of trade credits," Mboweni said.  \par \par \uc2 Mboweni made two pledges when he became the first black governor to take the post in 1999: not to use \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and to eliminate the bank's uncovered \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  liabilities.  \par \par \uc2 He achieved the second goal in May last year when the NOFP became a positive rather than a negative balance. Mboweni also vowed to close the forward book, which cost the country billions of dollars, and met this objective on February 18.  \par \par \uc2 The bank earlier said that its net open foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  position - the difference between its net reserves and forward book - fell to $3.962 billion from $4.774 billion in January, mostly because of the treasury's prepayment of $750 million in syndicated loans.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Ed Stoddard).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040301e0310019n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
