\par\par \b \uc2  Exporters rescue S.Africa rand from 4-month low. \b0\par\par\uc2 706 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2002\par 16:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, Aug 21 (Reuters) - Export orders brought South Africa's rand back from its weakest level in four months on Wednesday, after it took a hit from political turmoil in Zimbabwe. \par \par \uc2  The rand was down ten cents against the dollar at 10.85 at 1410 GMT, recovering from a four month low of 10.95 earlier in the day. At this level the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost 2.8 percent of its value over the last two days. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Zimbabwe's eviction of white farmers and the absence of public condemnation from domestic authorities - along with worse-than-expected inflation data on Tuesday - had hurt the rand, but exporters had halted the decline. \par \par \uc2  "The guys were looking to take the rand past 11 to the dollar, then this export order came in," one Johannesburg-based trader said. But he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would remain vulnerable to a further slide while it stayed in its current range. \par \par \uc2  "While it stays above 10.75-10.80, 11 (dollars) is still on the cards," he said. \par \par \uc2  "The feeling is that the rand will take out 11 quite soon," another trader added. \par \par \uc2  News that \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of its citizens caught up in Zimbabwe's land crisis was seen seen as a positive influence on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, a senior U.S. official said that Washington did not consider Zimbabwean President Robert Mugabe a legitimate leader and was working with South Africa, Botswana and Mozambique on ways to isolate him. \par \par \uc2  Mugabe is pushing ahead with his government's programme to resettle landless blacks, ordering 2,900 of the country's remaining 4,500 white commercial farmers to quit their land without compensation. \par \par \uc2  "It is general negative sentiment (that is hurting the rand), and what is happening in Zimbabwe is having a big effect," another trader said. \par \par \uc2  The rand began to wobble on Tuesday after news that inflation rose more than expected in July, although unfounded rumours that a Fitch outlook upgrade for South Africa was wrong were seen as the main trigger for breaks of key levels. \par \par \uc2  "We've created a new range between 10.78 and 11.05 in the short term...but I don't think we will weaken dramatically again," another trader said. \par \par \uc2  The rand's recovery in 2002 after a historic plunge of 37 percent against the U.S. unit late last year has been curbed by a combination of regional and global concerns. It hit a record low of 13.85 on December 20. \par \par \uc2  South African bond yields shadowed the rand, clawing back some of the ground lost earlier in the day, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The market has basically followed the rand," one trader said, adding that the interest rate curve had inverted a little further, with more buyer interest focussing on the long end of the curve. \par \par \uc2  Yields on the benchmark R153 due 2010 climbed 8.5 basis points to 11.46 percent, while the most traded R150 soared by 18.5 basis points to 11.515 percent. \par \par \uc2  Statistics South Africa said on Tuesday that the annual increase in the CPIX index targeted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for monetary policy accelerated to 9.9 percent in July from 9.8 percent in June - the fastest since its January 1997 debut. \par \par \uc2  Most economists remain convinced that the Reserve Bank would hold its fire on interest rates after raising them by three percentage points so far in 2002 to quash inflation ignited mainly by the rand's historic dive late last year. \par \par \uc2  But others believe another rate hike is becoming a real risk, particularly in light of climbing international oil prices. \par \par \uc2  For related prices and news \par \par \uc2  - ~- - - SOUTH AFRICAN PRICES \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    All S.African gilts              Benchmark R150\par    Rand Eurobonds                   Rand cross rates\par    Rand forwards                    Rand/dollar futures\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  - - - -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    All S.African news               S.African diary\par    All debt news                    S.African summary\par    S.African indicators             Index of summaries\par    Long-term forecasts              All African news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  - - - -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  EMERGING MARKET DEBT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Benchmark Brazil bond\par    Benchmark Argentine bond\par    Benchmark Mexican bond\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - ~- --\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For a complete list of Brady Bond prices on Reuters type 'BRADY' and\par hit the F3 key. Also see the emerging market speed guide by\par double-clicking on .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020821dy8l00s96\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
