\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-SAfrica c.bank moves highlighted in rand inquiry. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mariam Isa \par \uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 17:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, March 5 (Reuters) - Repeated comments from \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rand late in 2001 added to pressure on the depreciating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an official inquiry heard on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Rand Merchant Bank chief economist Rudolf Gouws told a commission investigating the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide that he believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance was correct, but the fact it was publicised helped convince markets the rand was a one-way bet. \par \par \uc2  Gouws was replying to a question at the inquiry set up by President Thabo Mbeki to probe the reasons for the rand's unprecedented 37 percent plunge against the dollar in 2001, mainly in the last weeks of the year. \par \par \uc2  The rand has since recovered by more than 22 percent from a record low of 13.85 against the U.S. unit on December 20, helped by a government policy statement and capital inflows from the sale of the government's stake in mobile operator M-Cell. \par \par \uc2  But domestic inflation has surged in response to the depreciation, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise interest rates unexpectedly in mid-January in a move seen as likely to curb already sluggish growth in the economy. \par \par \uc2  "I am in support of the Reserve Bank not trying to defend at all cost a pre-determined exchange rate," Gouws said. \par \par \uc2  "But by saying there would be no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rand seemed more of a one-way bet, especially with other things being negative. Some form of subtle \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or not such a strong stressing of this (non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) would have been helpful." \par \par \uc2  Late in November, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Tito Mboweni repeated his position that there was no target for the rand, as monetary policy is focused on the government's inflation target. \par \par \uc2  SENTIMENT SEEN KEY TO RAND \par \par \uc2  Mark Langley, former Treasury head of Credit Agricole Indosuez in Johannesburg, told the inquiry that sentiment was the most import factor driving the rand. Media coverage of the South African Reserve Bank's (SARB) stance on non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had compounded the negative view of the rand, he added. \par \par \uc2  "The combination of sentiment, the SARB'S action of draining liquidity, and foreign fund manager activity, which can amount to billions of dollars, can weigh dramatically on the rand." \par \par \uc2  He said that the only entity likely to benefit from the rand's abrupt plunge would be foreign fund managers. \par \par \uc2  He also said the SARB's decision to absorb all of a $3 billion inflow from Anglo American's buyout of De Beers in July had deprived the market of an inflow supportive to the rand. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took the step to further reduce its uncovered \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  liabilities - which was seen as the key obstacle to a sustained recovery in the volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In his testimony, Gouws stressed it was important to see the rand's fall in the perspective of a weakening bias in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2000 and an "extraordinary confluence" of factors which began to exert themselves from September onwards. \par \par \uc2  Mbeki set up the probe after South African Chamber of Business chairman Kevin Wakeford alleged there had been "dubious" manipulation of the markets. \par \par \uc2  Gouws said factors weighing on the rand included a flight to quality assets by global investors after September 11, news of a large \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  account deficit in the third quarter and a repo rate cut on September 20. \par \par \uc2  The government's decision to delay the partial sale of its majority stake in telecoms operator Telkom and the resulting slowdown in the unwinding of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's uncovered \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  liabilities were also factors, he noted. \par \par \uc2  Gouws also highlighted the South African Reserve Bank's decision to more rigidly enforce \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls in mid-October, which he said had scared many foreign players away from the market, resulting in sharp falls in liquidity. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020305dy3500wf9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
