\par\par \b \uc2  S.Africa c.bank moves highlighted in rand inquiry. \b0\par\par\uc2 576 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 13:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, March 5 (Reuters) - Repeated comments from \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rand late in 2001 added to pressure on the depreciating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an official inquiry heard on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Rand Merchant Bank chief economist Rudolf Gouws told a commission investigating the rand's slide that he believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance was correct, but the fact it was publicised helped convince markets the rand was a one-way bet. \par \par \uc2  Gouws was replying to a question at an offical inquiry set up by President Thabo Mbeki to probe the reasons for the rand's unprecedented slide of 37 percent against the dollar in 2001, which mainly took place in the final weeks of the year. \par \par \uc2  The rand has since recovered by more than 22 percent from a record low of 13.85 against the U.S. unit on December 20, helped by a government policy statement and capital inflows from the sale of the government's stake in mobile operator M-Cell. \par \par \uc2  "I am in support of the Reserve Bank not trying to defend at all cost a pre-determined exchange rate," Gouws said. \par \par \uc2  "But by saying there would be no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the rand seemed more of a one-way bet, especially with other things being negative. Some form of subtle \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or not such a strong stressing of this (non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) would have been helpful." \par \par \uc2  Late in November, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Tito Mboweni repeated his position that there was no target for the rand, as monetary policy is focused on the government's inflation target. \par \par \uc2  In his testimony, Gouws stressed that it was important to see the rand's fall in the perspective of a weakening bias in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2000 and an "extraordinary confluence" of factors which began to exert themselves from September onwards. \par \par \uc2  "To attribute the fall in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a number of specific transactions would therfore be very difficult and perhaps pointless in the light of the magnitude and complexity of developments since early September last year," he said. \par \par \uc2  Mbeki set up the probe after South African Chamber of Business chairman Kevin Wakeford alleged there had been "dubious" manipulation of the markets. \par \par \uc2  Gouws said factors weighing on the rand included a flight to quality assets by global investors after September 11, news of a large \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  account deficit in the third quarter and a repo rate cut on September 20. \par \par \uc2  The government's decision to delay the partial sale of its majority stake in telecoms operator Telkom and the resulting slowdown in the unwinding of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's uncovered \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  liabilities were also factors, he noted. \par \par \uc2  Gouws also highlighted the South African Reserve Bank's decision to more rigidly enforce \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls in mid-October, which he said had scared many foreign players away from the market, resulting in sharp falls in liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Turnover in the rand fell to around $5.5 billion a day in November and $6 billion in December from an average of more than $7 billion over the whole year, his data showed. \par \par \uc2  This helped exaggerate the impact of subsequent trades, as players scrambled to protect themselves from the risk of any further depreciation in the exchange rate, he said. \par \par \uc2  This led to exporters delaying the repatratiation of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings for as long as possible while importers hedged themselves against further falls in the rand. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020305dy3500pbg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
