\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  "no answer" for weak rand - Marcus. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sue Thomas \par \uc2 498 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2001\par 13:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, Oct 11 (Reuters) - South African deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Gill Marcus countered speculation the bank might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the weak rand saying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "not an answer" to the problem. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk flared last week when Reserve Bank Governor Tito Mboweni said it was an option, despite the Bank repeatedly ruling out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since 1999 because of inadequate reserves. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think there is any question of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the rand. Putting money into defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a losing streak," Marcus told a business seminar in Johannesburg on Thursday. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not an answer." \par \par \uc2  Her comments boosted the rand - which has lost 18 percent versus the dollar this year on political and economic turmoil in neighbouring Zimbabwe and the contagion effect of emerging market ills - because \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders agree that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would saddle \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy with extra borrowing. \par \par \uc2  "I agree with Marcus' sentiments. At the end of the day we don't have the reserves to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We're too small a country," said Mike Schussler, an economist at stock broking firm Tradek. \par \par \uc2  "But the weaker rand gives us an advantage and exports should grow. The rand will find an automatic stabiliser. With the global economy slowing, now is not the time to have a strong rand," Schussler added. \par \par \uc2  The rand rose to 9.1650 against the greenback versus Wednesday's closing level of 9.18, before dipping back slightly to 9.1775 at 0922 GMT. The latest gains came after the rand cracked key overhead resistance in overnight trade. \par \par \uc2  "The market has taken the comments by Marcus as positive. The market doesn't need \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dollars will naturally flow in at certain rates," said one foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. \par \par \uc2  DEPRECIATION PERVASIVE \par \par \uc2  Marcus said the rand was totally undervalued and that there was no reason for a lack of confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation is very pervasive and it's about the uncertainties in the world. The problem is when other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recover the rand doesn't quite follow," Marcus said. \par \par \uc2  Marcus pointed to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashing its so-called net open forward position (NOFP) - in effect a dollar overdraft built up by the bank in a vain attempt to prop up the rand - from 23 billion dollars in 1998 to 4.8 billion dollars currently. \par \par \uc2  The NOFP has been an obstacle to the rand's recovery because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must buy dollars regularly to maintain the dollar overdraft. Mboweni said last Friday it was now small enough to get rid of. \par \par \uc2  Also on Friday, Mboweni said of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 : "In the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fraternity...it is well known that amongst the tools at our disposal is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Central banks use those tools as and when they want to," Mboweni told the finance committee of the provincial Gauteng legislature. \par \par \uc2  "Sometimes they do it in such a way that no one notices," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011011dxab00eyy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
