\par\par \b \uc2  S.Africa's Manuel says won't  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in rand fall. \b0\par\par\uc2 449 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2001\par 15:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CAPE TOWN, Sept 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister Trevor Manuel expressed his exasperation on Wednesday over consistent attacks on the rand, but reaffirmed that the government would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We don't have the kind of reserves even if we wanted to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against attack," Manuel said at a media briefing after a closed-door conference in Cape Town. \par \par \uc2  He added it was government's policy that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to prop up the rand. Economists say that the strategy is a sensible one given the fact that it has seldom been effective in the past. \par \par \uc2  Manuel said the government should be given credit for reducing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's net open forward position (NOFP), seen as the Achilles heel of the rand, from about $24 billion (in 1998) to the current $4.8 billion. \par \par \uc2  The NOFP is a measure of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's uncovered \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure and is an obstacle to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recovery because it means the Reserve Bank must buy regularly dollars to maintain the position. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether he believed the rand was undervalued Manuel replied: "We can't talk value for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but we want to plead for rationality." \par \par \uc2  South Africa's rand has hit successive lows against key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past few weeks, taking its losses on a trade weighted basis this to almost nine percent. It has fallen by about 12 percent against the dollar since the start of 2001. \par \par \uc2  Manuel said he could not see any particular threat to the South African economy arising out of Tuesday's attacks on the World Trade Centre in New York and the Pentagon. \par \par \uc2  "The key question is what happens to oil prices," he said. \par \par \uc2  "No single country can insulate itself from global trends, but what we have going for us is that our exports are more diversified than they have ever been," he added. \par \par \uc2  Stubbornly high oil prices are seen as the main threat to the government's three to six percent inflation target introduced last year. The targeted CPIX index rose by 6.4 percent in the year to July, unchanged from June. \par \par \uc2  Economists also say that a sharp slowdown in the U.S. economy would take its toll on South Africa's relatively sluggish rate of growth. \par \par \uc2  The United States accounts for between 11 and 15 percent of South Africa's exports, Trade and Industry Minister Alec Erwin said. \par \par \uc2  "We will be hurt on commodity exports like steel and we might get some benefit on gold," Erwin told the same media briefing. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx9c019p7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
