\par\par \b \uc2  S.Africa bonds yields fall heavily, rand supported. \b0\par\par\uc2 908 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2000\par 15:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  1415 GMT - South African bonds yields fall to their lowest level since April 1998 on back of strong local institutional and bank demand prompted by change in exchange's tracker index. Rand briefly supported after another round of euro \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by ECB and strong bond buying. \par \par \uc2  * Yield on benchmark R150 government bond, due 2005, falls heavily to trade at low of 12.475 pct from 12.71 pct at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  * R150 last bid at 12.52 pct. \par \par \uc2  * R150s broke through key resistance at 12.64 pct, 12.58 pct and 12.50 pct. Hit 12.41 pct in April 1998. \par \par \uc2  * R153s last bid at 13.21 pct from 13.39 pct close. Interest spurred by dropping of ZAR162s out of index, traders said. \par \par \uc2  * Rand last bid at 7.527 to dollar from 7.53 after news of ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Euro - the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main trading partners - last at $0.8665 from $0.8632 prior to ECB move. Hit as high as $0.8730 on ECB euro buying. \par \par \uc2  * On crosses, at 10.83 against pound from 10.88 at opening. Bid at 6.50 vs euro from 6.51 opening. \par \par \uc2  * Bond yields also supported by Treasury's successful first switch auction as market puts to one side inflationary concerns, traders said. \par \par \uc2  * Treasury bought back 460 million rand of its R177 bond, due May 2007, for 375.369 million rand of its R157 bond, due September 2014/15/16, in its first switch auction . Bids totalled 2.06 billion rand. \par \par \uc2  * "The demand for longer-term debt remains marked," said one Johannesburg-based trader. \par \par \uc2  * Reserve Bank sold one billion rand's worth of the government's benchmark R150 bonds via a reverse repo auction at an average rate of 10.26 percent. Bank also sold 250 million rand of R186 bonds at an average reverse repo rate of 10.40 pct. \par \par \uc2  South Africa's debt market shone on Monday as local investors piled into government bonds while the beleaguered rand found support after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the sickly euro. \par \par \uc2  The yield on government's benchmark five-year R150 bond - which moves in an opposite direction to the price - traded as low as 12.48 percent, down from its 12.71 percent close on Friday. \par \par \uc2  It hit its lowest yield since April 1998 after breaking through key resistance levels at 12.58 percent, according to Reuters Graphics. Traders saw 12.38 percent as the next target. \par \par \uc2  Heavy buying in bonds, weaker oil prices - easing inflationary pressures - and renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Frankfurt-based ECB also helped support the volatile rand which pulled back some of the 24 percent it has lost against the dollar this year. \par \par \uc2  The rand traded as strong as 7.49 to the dollar as the euro - the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of South Africa's major trading partners - rallied nearly a cent against the dollar after the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a second consecutive trading day. \par \par \uc2  The rand was last bid at 7.51 to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from 7.53 late on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The bond rally, which came despite inflation concerns, was partly a defensive move out of a sagging stock market but also a decisive move by local institutions and banks to compensate for a change in Johannesburg's key bond exchange index, traders said. \par \par \uc2  A revision in the domestic bond index prompted local traders to seek R157, due 2015, and R150 bonds to replace R162 bonds, due 2002, which have been dropped out of the Bond Exchange's tracking index. \par \par \uc2  "The focus has been on the R157s," said Tim Marsland, head of fixed income at ABN-Amro. \par \par \uc2  The R157 was last bid at 13.365 percent. \par \par \uc2  Investor interest in longer-term government debt was also shown in a move by the Treasury to improve domestic debt liquidity in a successful switch auction for primary dealers. \par \par \uc2  The switch, used by the Reserve Bank for the first time to swap debt maturing in 2007 on its R177 bond for its R157 bond, was well received by the market which bid strongly for longer-term script. \par \par \uc2  "The auction was a successful one. It showed demand from local institutions for the long-end of the market remains marked," said Marilyn Visser, director of fixed income at HSBC Securities in South Africa. \par \par \uc2  The treasury bought back 460 million rand of its R177 bond in the switch \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange for 375.36 million rand of its R157 bond. Bids totalled over two billion rand . \par \par \uc2  Leon Myburgh at Barclays said: "The market easily absorbed the duration lengthening and that is a positive sign...The short term outlook for yields is therefore still favourable." \par \par \uc2  Improved debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets also helped ease market fears of the Reserve Bank tightening its monetary policy at its next monetary policy committee meeting on November 15-16. \par \par \uc2  The bank surprised markets last month when it announced a 25 basis point rise in its key repo rate - the first rise since the emerging markets crisis of 1998 - as a pre-emptive strike against inflationary pressures and to bolster a sagging rand. \par \par \uc2  "The bank is probably satisfied that the psychological effect of its rate hike has sufficiently contained the risk of secondary price effects on wages and supply contracts," said Standard Bank in a market commentary. \par \par \uc2  For related prices and news Also see the emerging market speed guide by double-clicking on . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb602o10\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
