\par\par \b \uc2  S. African bank official sees few ways to boost rand. \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2000\par 01:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MONTREAL, Oct 23 (Reuters) - A senior South African \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Monday that the rand, hovering near record lows against the U.S. dollar, had fallen victim to the greenback's strength and there was little policy makers could do to reverse the move. \par \par \uc2  "We have said publicly that we would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Timothy Thahane, deputy governor of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2  said at the start of a top level international meeting in Montreal where rich and poor countries will discuss ways to strengthen the world's financial system. He shrugged his shoulders when asked what the next step might be. \par \par \uc2  With the rand bid at just over 7.58 against the U.S. dollar, still near last Wednesday's record low of 7.71, Thahane said, "The situation with the rand is more of a function of the strength of the dollar than anything else." \par \par \uc2  Because South Africa's main trading \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the euro, which has fallen more than 25 percent against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since it was launched in January 1999, and last week hit a record low, the rand has followed the euro's volatile moves. \par \par \uc2  Asked what South Africa's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might do to combat the rand's weakness Thahane declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked its key lending rate by 25 basis points to 12.0 percent. While the move was not enough to make commercial banks follow suit, it sent a strong signal that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prepared to tighten monetary policy in a bid to slow inflationary pressures brought on by higher oil prices and the weaker rand. \par \par \uc2  Thahane said exchange rates were not on the agenda at this meeting when the group's finance ministers and central bankers are scheduled to meet on Tuesday and Wednesday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwan03h9o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
