\par\par \b \uc2  S.Africa c.bnk says not  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  mkt. \b0\par\par\uc2 187 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2000\par 14:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  JOHANNESBURG, Sept 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Africa\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Reserve Bank said on Monday that it was not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to protect the rand, which has fallen to a succession of new lows against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said that the weakness in the rand was a reflection of dollar strength rather than a fundamental problem with the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We are certainly not selling dollars in defence of the rand," Bertus van Zyl, general manager of international banking at the bank told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "This (rand weakness) is a reflection of dollar strength against euro and sterling," van Zyl said. \par \par \uc2  The rand fell one percent from levels seen on Friday to a fresh record low of 7.2720 to the dollar, taking its slide against the U.S. unit this year to 17 percent. \par \par \uc2  Reserve Bank governor Tito Mboweni has repeatedly said it would not make sense for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to use its limited foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to defend the rand, a policy which economists say has helped support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9i07dtz\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\